:"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106316#post1106316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Inanamorta are apparent reincarnations (appearance-wise) of a vampire's lost loves whose blood is effectively Kindred Marijuana-it causes them to be cheerfully high on &amp;quot;life&amp;quot; for a while and debuffs their Disciplines, already hazardous were it not for the fact that while high, the vampire has a tendency to think he's sun-proof. Empusas/Lamiae are effectively strange divergent clans of Kindred who lack Touchstones (though not Humanity), TWDND and Dvora are the same person, an immortal vampire huntress and patron of hunters, and King Kitamba is an immortal man who sacrifices vampires to maintain his life (and interestingly, honor his long-dead wife).</div> </div> </div> </div> Changeling blood is like pot, Inanamorta blood is like an amped up blush of life that you don't have to spend vitae for at the cost of weaken disciplines, devotions, the urge to walk Out into the sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T04:34:47-07:00","id":1106485,"title":"","content":"The Methuselahs section massively disappointed me. It goes into how they have all this time to develop things elders can barely touch upon, but then gives them no unique mechanics and nothing but the elder devotions in the book. So, basically... as presented they're absolutely no different from any other elder, at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T05:19:29-07:00","id":1106498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106460#post1106460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ann Harlow, Daeva Methuselah, Strength 7, no Vigor.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least it's viable since she's BP 8. Check out Jack the Draugr who has Survival 8 and BP 7. He also has Celerity 7. Also, the only derived trait that actually matches his Attributes and Skills is Willpower. Health, Speed, Initiative and Defense seems to have been arbitrarily stated instead of being derived.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T05:49:31-07:00","id":1106501,"title":"","content":"The can the Inamorata be embraced or ghouled? I mean obviously if you do so they probably stop being Inamorata.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 06-22-2017, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T05:53:06-07:00","id":1106504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106501#post1106501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The can the Inamorata be embraced or ghouled? I mean obviously if you do so they probably stop being Inanorata.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nothing on this subject in the book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T06:38:15-07:00","id":1106517,"title":"","content":"One thing I realized with the Akhud being a true clan here now, is that any Vampire with access to Akhud blood would be able to learn Praestantia, and that Bloodlines should be able to manifest it, just as they can with other clan-specific Disciplines. (Such as Kerberos being granted Majesty).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T06:41:12-07:00","id":1106519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106517#post1106517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I realized with the Akhud being a true clan here now, is that any Vampire with access to Akhud blood would be able to learn Praestantia, and that Bloodlines should be able to manifest it, just as they can with other clan-specific Disciplines. (Such as Kerberos being granted Majesty).</div> </div> </div> </div>I was wondering that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T06:51:34-07:00","id":1106526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106517#post1106517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I realized with the Akhud being a true clan here now, is that any Vampire with access to Akhud blood would be able to learn Praestantia, and that Bloodlines should be able to manifest it, just as they can with other clan-specific Disciplines. (Such as Kerberos being granted Majesty).</div> </div> </div> </div> The Akhud also aren't automatically members of VII, so they could join any covenant. <br /> <br /> An Akhud Crone could be interesting because their Void Creatures and Blood Gods could have Praestantia. ghouls too.<br /> <br /> Also, how do you pronounce Praestantia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T07:33:50-07:00","id":1106540,"title":"","content":"Is it me or are Pijavica kinda meh? You can't even really play one before hiting ancilae or elder","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T08:01:51-07:00","id":1106547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106526#post1106526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, how do you pronounce Praestantia?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://forvo.com/word/la/praestantia/\" target=\"_blank\">https://forvo.com/word/la/praestantia/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T08:05:29-07:00","id":1106552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106485#post1106485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Methuselahs section massively disappointed me. It goes into how they have all this time to develop things elders can barely touch upon, but then gives them no unique mechanics and nothing but the elder devotions in the book. So, basically... as presented they're absolutely no different from any other elder, at all.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, it does say that they get to wake up from torpor without losing BP. But, yeah, that's about it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T08:05:29-07:00","id":1106553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106517#post1106517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I realized with the Akhud being a true clan here now, is that any Vampire with access to Akhud blood would be able to learn Praestantia, and that Bloodlines should be able to manifest it, just as they can with other clan-specific Disciplines. (Such as Kerberos being granted Majesty).</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on the fluff it doesn't seem like a 'normal' Discipline, just like the Akhud are not normal vampires. It's a tradeoff for the diablerist taint. Though obviously nothing keeps you from using it as a standard Discipline.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T08:25:24-07:00","id":1106568,"title":"","content":"its a bit of a knee jerk reaction but i really don't like the Spontaneous Combustion devotion, it just seems incredible against theme to be able to naturally produce one of your banes. Is this just me and am I being too narrow minded or does anyone else have similar misgivings?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T08:30:34-07:00","id":1106570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WelshBoi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106568#post1106568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">its a bit of a knee jerk reaction but i really don't like the Spontaneous Combustion devotion, it just seems incredible against theme to be able to naturally produce one of your banes. Is this just me and am I being too narrow minded or does anyone else have similar misgivings?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the method it does it makes sense. It's not like breathing or channeling fire from your soul. And the strangeness of it is offset by the large Vitae cost.<br /> <br /> You should probably be able to get a discount if you announce, 'Flash Fact' and describe what you're doing as you do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-22-2017, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T08:59:46-07:00","id":1106586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106552#post1106552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, it does say that they get to wake up from torpor without losing BP. But, yeah, that's about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing you're refering to this sentence:<br /> <br /> &quot;Methuselahs remember back to those early nights, and, though they may have spent decades or centuries in the deep sleep of torpor, they awaken as powerful as they were when they first closed their eyes.&quot;<br /> <br /> It doesn't actually say anything. You can just as well interpret that as Methuselahs keeping access to their 6+ Traits and Elder Devotions. I think that's the intended reading.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My biggest grievance with this book (along with Ancient Mysteries and Ancient Bloodlines) is that I have a completely different idea of what an Elder is supposed to be. When someone says Elder I start thinking about vampires who's already been through Torpor due to age at least once. Not 200 year olds who can still feed from humans (unless they've been especially active or have diablerized others).<br /> Eight out of ten eras in Ancient Mysteries/Bloodlines are less than 1000 years old. Five and a half era is less than 500 years old. Three of them happened within 200 years from modern days. That's very, very far from ancient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T09:08:27-07:00","id":1106595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106586#post1106586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest grievance with this book (along with Ancient Mysteries and Ancient Bloodlines) is that I have a completely different idea of what an Elder is supposed to be. When someone says Elder I start thinking about vampires who's already been through Torpor due to age at least once. Not 200 year olds who can still feed from humans (unless they've been especially active or have diablerized others).</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you know where you got that idea from? Is it a Masquerade thing? Elders are vampires who have spent 150 years or more in undeath since the first Requiem book but I'm not sure the age terms for Masquerade ones. I thought generation was more important. Even then I can understand your issue, but it shouldn't be a problem. The book one supports 150 year old vampires who still feed off of humans as well as 1000 year old elders who've lived a variety of other lives and who seemingly spawn new sorceries at a whim. If you don't count them as elders until a certain age, then don't make them at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-22-2017, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T09:14:16-07:00","id":1106598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106595#post1106595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you know where you got that idea from? Is it a Masquerade thing? Elders are vampires who have spent 150 years or more in undeath since the first Requiem book but I'm not sure the age terms for Masquerade ones. I thought generation was more important. Even then I can understand your issue, but it shouldn't be a problem. The book one supports 150 year old vampires who still feed off of humans as well as 1000 year old elders who've lived a variety of other lives and who seemingly spawn new sorceries at a whim. If you don't count them as elders until a certain age, then don't make them at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, in Vampire Lexicon we can find that Ancilla have 50-150 years of Requiem and Elders have 150+","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T09:17:05-07:00","id":1106602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orzhov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106540#post1106540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it me or are Pijavica kinda meh? You can't even really play one before hiting ancilae or elder</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that's why they died out. Neonates are really, really vulnerable to attrition, on the basis that those without Humanity are morons. Still though, it isn't that bad-the Pijavica just needs to keep to the wild places to feed on animals until BP 3-when their mental problems aren't nearly as bad. <br /> <br /> Still, I would make them all have very high starting dots in Protean, as they're literally blobs of sentient, malleable blood. It flows naturally to them, pardon the pun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T09:25:50-07:00","id":1106608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106602#post1106602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's why they died out. Neonates are really, really vulnerable to attrition, on the basis that those without Humanity are morons. Still though, it isn't that bad-the Pijavica just needs to keep to the wild places to feed on animals until BP 3-when their mental problems aren't nearly as bad.<br /> <br /> Still, I would make them all have very high starting dots in Protean, as they're literally blobs of sentient, malleable blood. It flows naturally to them, pardon the pun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they fit in best in Dark Eras, and it's easier to imagine them in the Neolithic or even Pangaea. Not just because of the readily available animal blood but because people can't really organize a defense as well. They offer some interesting tactics, too, just turning their arms to blood and shoving it into someone's mouth to get them blood bound.<br /> <br /> Though the 'last' one and his attempts to revitalize the clan are a solid modern nights story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T09:27:49-07:00","id":1106611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106602#post1106602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's why they died out. Neonates are really, really vulnerable to attrition, on the basis that those without Humanity are morons. Still though, it isn't that bad-the Pijavica just needs to keep to the wild places to feed on animals until BP 3-when their mental problems aren't nearly as bad.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Well in the context of the book this is less of a problem because you start at BP5 and so at fullstrengtht. However there seems to be more downside to playing pijavica than its worth. Maybe should get some devotions to alleviatee that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T09:32:53-07:00","id":1106615,"title":"","content":"How Methuselahs are defined in <b>Requiem</b> now? In <b>Masquerade</b> they have really low Generation - i.e. coming (almost) straight from Cain - but in <b>Requiem </b>there is no single canonical source of vampirism. So what are Methuselahs here? First members of particular Clan, like Progenitors from <b>Promethean</b>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T09:36:03-07:00","id":1106617,"title":"","content":"So, I've finished reading the book, and here's my thoughts.<br /> <br /> <b>I. Cover and Opening Fiction.</b><br /> While not -wow- over the cover, its a good picture. The opening fiction is nice. Flows well. I kind of wondered why the elder daeva embraced that childer in the first place when its clear he's got a lack of common sense. Still, I like the story of how the poker game flowed, using it as a testing of each other. The ending was amusing, and admittedly a twist that I wasn't quite expecting. An entire conversation through the game. I even like the buck-tooth Nosferatu picture.<br /> <br /> <b>II. Chapter 1 - Opening Moments</b><br /> Well, first let me say this - I find the xp distribution to be rather shallow. Disappointing mechanics is a common refrain I have throughout this book. The &quot;example elders&quot; were kind of boring to me - just a few small skill and attribute bumps, and merits. This feels more like how to make an experienced -mortal- rather than a vampire, no real considerations for vampire's nature or abilities in the write ups.<br /> <br /> That aside? Lets get into the real meat of the discussion. Character creation. We're being walked through, step by step, how to make an elder game, what considerations to make to the thought process behind each age. Which is admittedly pretty cool. I like the emphasis on early days defining a vampire throughout their Requiem. It reminds me of how your first three years as a child basically shape your entire life. Yay formative years! Far too often, we do get lost in the age and supposed power of an elder, but bringing back the focus to, yes, that first human scent is good. I love the idea of a faded touchstone, highlighting this entire thing perfectly.<br /> <br /> Portrayal of clans. Now this is pretty interesting. I especially like the lost clans - that was a welcome surprise I did NOT expect to see. I also am in love with the idea of elder curses (which are one of the mechanics I do adore). I'm not quite sure on the Nosferatu one (lets drop humanity fast!), but that's because it seems to make them, well, haunts. Very lair-oriented. The problem being that it makes them unlikely to leave said lair. The Ventrue one is particuarly inspired, I think, though, and I will probably swap this one with the regular one. The base five clan writeups themselves were good, and, while nothing ground breaking, they're good directions to read up on and gives good considerations to how you adapt while keeping anachronisms.<br /> <br /> Side note - I'm still not understanding what the picture of the guy holding his bleeding arm, and the woman on the ground holding her head screaming, gun next to her. Page 28. Is that supposed to be overloaded senses? The Curse of Five coming into play?<br /> <br /> And we get to the first part of the book's fluff I'm not liking. I feel like the covenant section is basically summed up as &quot;you get cults of personality, flavored by covenant philosophy.&quot; Or &quot;go off on your own.&quot; I don't feel there's much here to explore beyond &quot;trusted elders = leadership roles.&quot; And I also feel like we're dealing more with the 1e covenants rather than the expanded 2e. I loved the different flavors of the Circle we saw in Secrets, but here? Back to the pseud-wicca Mother-Maiden-Crone bits. No references to the Invictus as the Masquerade enforces, just as Establishment. Dynasty is listed under Invictus again, despite the core pushing it towards clan-based (Also - The reference to dynasty oath could use a page reference, or something, as I was getting it confused with the core book merit). Dynasties have nothing to do with covenant! If anything, it should have been under Clan! And that sidebar! Dynasties are already cross covenant by nature. Its utterly meaningless.<br /> <br /> Cerberus pact feels like a variation on VII. Which might have been the intent - playable VII that doesn't tell you what the VII are. Its got its appeal, but I'm still not sure why we're going with elder-only, however. I don't feel anything elder-ish about the Pact.<br /> <br /> <b>III. The Long Solo</b><br /> We start with a small thing about why vampires prize memories and &quot;transcend history.&quot; Feel like there's references to how Ancient books talked about vampire history. Cool. Vampire elders want to make a mark on the world and not be forgotten. Okay. Ah, Flashback scenes. Now this is tasty. Not a fan of all the Masquerade-era &quot;vampires fear change&quot; leaking in, but ideas for going back in history is nice. Nothing immediately useful outside of an elder game, but solid ideas on what to focus on. I like structuring it on idfferent themes like love or intrigue or the Embrace. Nothing really stands out to me, but that's because I dont have an immediate need for it. I can see the definite value during future games, however.<br /> <br /> <b>IV. What we Learned Along the Way</b><br /> Aww... first chapter title not related to music. Sadness. So, we have a section on 6+ attributes. Okay. I don't understand why its unique to elders, when its basically something that all vampires experince through disciplines. Wits made me feel like it was talking about an Auspex user. Strength and Stamina above 5 are common with disciplines, and they can't be turned off. Bits of things about &quot;superhuman attributes are noticable Masquerade breaches.&quot; Honestly, its a good bit of discussion for any game that lets you get over 5+ stuff. I'm probably going to use it for mages and why stats 5+ cause issues with Dissonance too. Its a good discussion to have, and kind of important. &quot;Here's how you role play a high stat character.&quot; Something anyone routinely pushing themselves past 5 in a stat should read, and I'm glad its here, for every game out there.<br /> <br /> The same with skills. You see this all the time with people in different fields, let alone supernaturally advanced mastery. I'm currently playing a high occult character in changeling, with supernatural means of boosting my actual score to around the equivalent of 8 dice. Just from occult alone. I'm finding this pretty handy for how my character already. Again, another good read for anyone with supernaturally enhanced stats. Not groundbreaking, but excellent reference.<br /> <br /> I found the whole devotion section a bit confusing. So, learning devotions is difficult for vampires, because they need teachers or something? They make it sound like learning a devotion is a giant ordeal akin to learning rare blood sorceries, which is kind of at odds with how the core book describes the devotions. I get it, we want storyhooks, but I have to fall back to the core book here. As for the devotions themselves? Kind of neat, some of them. I like the Auspex one. For the most part, while expensive in terms of vitae, these are actually abilities everyone could learn or take, not just elders. I'd expect elder devotions to have a Blood Potency restriction, like they did in 1e. In terms of direct power? Honestly, I think the semi-official devotions that were supposed to be in Secrets via dropbox are stronger.<br /> <br /> Also? Vampires now have a pseudo-fire ability (Spontaneous Ignition) as well as telekinesis (Unbridled Force). I'm not sure if Unbridled Force can be used to fly or not, but I'd allow it. These devotions, while not powerful and often clunky, are at least iconic abilties that are nice to see. The only thing missing now is an icy aura, blood manipulation and venom fangs.<br /> <br /> Elder sorcery is apparently restricted in terms of age, but that's more of a social construct than ability. Much like the devotions above, there's a prohibitive cost associated with them, doubling the necessary willpower or vitae for some reason. Not really seeing the point, since most of the regular costs have built in offsets. But, as above, not a fan of this books mechanics for the most part. As for the rituals themselves? Detached limbs that can run around are always fun. I do like. 10 vitae and 10 successes to animate trees for the night? Less useful given the time invested. Maybe if we absolutely know there's going to be an attack on one's Mandrake garden on a certain night. Or set up an ambush. That said, it also seems to be attacking the ritualist? Scapegoat... just not a fan of the magical implications of being able to avoid derangements. You take derangements if you learn about something you did under frenzy later. Yet &quot;because magic&quot; you get to go crazy and do whatever without problem. Theban's Curse of Isolation has issues - putting aside things like forests or tombs as touchstones, but it doesn't touch on things like Impression, or if we're dealing with transfered feelings or anything. Very clunky. What happens when someone uses this against a True Friend touchstone? Or a faded touchstone? Orison of Voices is cool - you get to hear prayers directed to you. Not really worth a five dot ritual, especially when we have merits for regnants appearing in trouble. Cool, but should have been a merit with a Theban prerequisite. Sins of the Ancestors feels like it should be an Auspex power, and is of dubious use. Iconic, I suppose, but not something I see come up in play often, either for PCs or NPCs.<br /> <br /> Coil of the Quintessence. There's some implications here. 1) we can extend one of the three core coils by attaching a new Coil to a Mystery. 2) A coil built around territory control means we can have coils that do more than affect the vampire itself. Still a bit weak in terms of actual mechanics - Smother (and Cold of the Grave by extension) and Forever Mine are good. Everything else is questionable, imho.<br /> <br /> Merits - While I get the intent of most of these merits, I just can't see them being used. They sound good in theory, but in execution, I just don't see the benefit for the cost. Like... Major Domo. Its benefit is roughly equal to a two dot Status or Striking Looks merit but costs 3, has a drawback, and affects less social rolls. Married by Blood - a one dot merit that has a drawback, but lets you share Haven and Retainer dots, which you pretty much could do already? Well, maybe not Retainer, but Haven definitely already could. Plus, we have a marriage Oath already, which is far more powerful for the same cost. Whomever wrote these mechanics love the 9-again rule.<br /> <br /> Now, there are a few good options - using Receptive Mind for multiple Auspex 4 use is nice. Undeniable Aura is a thing; it has its downsides, but its pretty nifty overall. Special Treat is a trap tactic for getting someone else in trouble, or whoring out the blood as a drug for favors (mental note, never feed from a ghoul, even if offered). But most I don't care for as unnecessary.<br /> <br /> Carthian Law - Stare Decisis. Well, makes for a good carthian lawyer ability. But at this point in one's undead life, willpower shouldn't be hard to come by. The main use is in making other people waste resources fighting you socially. Has its uses in some games.<br /> <br /> Dynasty Merits - So, Dynastic Progenitor can be cool. Flat dice bonus to discipline use, but sure. Oath of Dynasty... Dynasties are not made, nor confirmed, by Notories. You already share blood sympathy with everyone, because you're all part of the same clan to begin with! Talking with torpid members is already done via Speaker for the Silent. I'm sorry, but I feel like whomever wrote this section on Dynasties was stuck with the old Invictus book instead of how the actual merits work in 2e. I feel like this Oath of Dynasty was meant to be the book's Invictus Oath. But, it doesn't even lean towards that.<br /> <br /> <b>V. What We Learned Along The Way</b><br /> Still sad we're done with music references in title. Moving on. So, we get to Spinning the Web. There's been references to this all over the place. So, now we finally see it. In brief, its a long list on how to roleplay your elder, and to help flesh out his history (revised by others), and all the little quirks. All in all, a very handy tool to have in terms of writing storyhooks. Always good to have as a reference. I particularly liked The Queen is Dead, Long Live the Queen.<br /> <br /> Touchstones get a bit of look at, but in another way - faux Touchstones that work differently. Its definitely an interesting take to reflect things, especially when combined with phantom touchstones. I'm pleased with tthe variety of touchstones presented in the book. The Halfway Port: Ghouls at least firmly establishes ghouls as potential touchstones, and not as human company. Discusses ghouls in an elder's life, though not in too much detail. Probably could have skipped this in favor of the half-damned book. The Death Barge: Revenants... I'm not sure what's going on here. &quot;There but for the Grace of God...&quot; Huh? Isn't that a draugr? Outcasts? They can be uplifted fairly easily, and wanted to by most cities, I imagine. Revenants are used to track sloppy feeders. Maybe serving as a touchstone? Wha? Given the next section on vampires, you can have other vampires a kind of faux touchstone... huh. I admit to skimming this part, as there's just too much to really focus on.<br /> <br /> <b>VI Wolves at the Gate.</b><br /> A picture of someone pulling an Emperor Palpatine on another. I presume this is a mage doing the lightning bit, given the sigils on her palms. The victim isn't a vampire (no fangs). Go figure why its in a vampire book. Its well done, but... how is this Vamipre? I guess a reference to the crossover section, but still.<br /> <br /> So, monsters that hunt the Kindred.<br /> Inamorata are a cruel twist - the dead coming back to haunt the undead. Lots of potential to be almost anything. Is it the dead lover? Is it a kind of shapeshifter that wants to destroy vampires? Angels? Other vampires? Ghosts (x-over with GtSE!)? Can be fun to play out, much like a Hollow Mehket's shadow can be.<br /> <br /> Draugr - powerful monsters, but more of a mirror than any kind of threat. You can run a kind of search-and-destroy game, but those tend to be over pretty fast, in my experience. No Prince wants a walking Masquerade breach hunting the streets of their city. And then, you have responces by Task Force Valkerie and other hunters, let alone other supernaturals. I can't imagine that they're a threat for an elder game. I'd also suggest reading up on them in the Gangrel book more.<br /> <br /> Empusa and Lamia - alternate vampires. Night Horros Dead Wicked style non-Kindred vampires. Basically, though, they're just glorified vampires who hunt vampires. I have to recommend using the Night Horrors books instead of these girls.<br /> <br /> Methuselahs are just old elders that don't lose BP in torpor. Not much to talk about here. Other than Ezekiel. Founder of the Akhud clan owning a PI firm is amusing, but not scary. And why does a ghoul have Blood Potency? I must have missed that being mentioned. Or its a typo. Same with the Lost Clans section - sample elder threats. 'Nough said.<br /> <br /> Body of a Nation - tier 3 global threats for elders in the form of Danse Macabre Conspiracy?<br /> <br /> Immortals:<br /> Deborah - basically, an immortal hunter, with a Compact/Conspiriacy based on her family, using psychic abilities.<br /> King Kitamba - another immortal hunter that may as well be a rogue ghoul with a slightly better time frame between feedings.<br /> Sons of Phobos - reprint from Blood Sorcery book, basically.<br /> <br /> Crossover section - notes on immortal mages (liches), long lived 'lings, and more. The only thing I'm going to mention is that no, Auras aren't how Auspex work anymore. Not really a fan of crossover, so skipping over.<br /> <br /> All in all, I can't say I'm impressed with this chapter. Feels like its just taking existing things and putting more stats on them. Same things as the neonate, just hits harder.<br /> <br /> <b>VII In Conclusion</b><br /> <br /> So. There you go. Basically, we have some very good ideas that go into the thought process of being an elder, how to build up history, some really good story hooks, new Touchstone ideas, and the occasional devotion worth having. <br /> <br /> If youw ant to do an elder game and need help getting into the mindset, good book to get. If you want it for the mechanics or antagonists? I suggest checking elsewhere.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-22-2017, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T09:37:22-07:00","id":1106618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106615#post1106615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How Methuselahs are defined in <b>Requiem</b> now? In <b>Masquerade</b> they have really low Generation - i.e. coming (almost) straight from Cain - but in <b>Requiem </b>there is no single canonical source of vampirism. So what are Methuselahs here? First members of particular Clan, like Progenitors from <b>Promethean</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>A thousand years or older. It's not a common term in Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T09:46:29-07:00","id":1106621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orzhov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106540#post1106540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it me or are Pijavica kinda meh? You can't even really play one before hiting ancilae or elder</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my first instinct, but then I took a look at the math. If you started as a Neonate with Humanity 7, a fairly standard assumption, about 92% of the time, you'll be using your full dicepool. It will certainly be really annoying when you get hit with the Pijavica Bane, but far from crippling. As long as you keep Humanity at 6 or above (88%), I don't think it should be too much of an issue. The result is that Humanity is even more important for Pijavica than most Kindred, which seems thematically appropriate, given how divorced they are are from humanity as sentient blood blobs.<br /> <br /> Weird, very. Unplayable, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 06-22-2017, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T11:01:25-07:00","id":1106646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106595#post1106595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you know where you got that idea from? Is it a Masquerade thing? Elders are vampires who have spent 150 years or more in undeath since the first Requiem book but I'm not sure the age terms for Masquerade ones. I thought generation was more important. Even then I can understand your issue, but it shouldn't be a problem. The book one supports 150 year old vampires who still feed off of humans as well as 1000 year old elders who've lived a variety of other lives and who seemingly spawn new sorceries at a whim. If you don't count them as elders until a certain age, then don't make them at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right that Requiem is consistent with what constitutes an Elder. So it's not specifically this book that I disagree with. It's just more relevant with this book. I just find those numbers to be quite underwhelming.<br /> <br /> I haven't played Masquerade, if that's what you're alluding to, but everyone in my group has, and I'm probably somewhat influenced by them since we've met several Elders in our campaign that have been in Torpor due to advanced BP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T11:07:03-07:00","id":1106649,"title":"","content":"The fluff is nice if strange in places. The section on attributes / skills is useful. The mechanics are pretty meh overall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T11:12:37-07:00","id":1106653,"title":"","content":"Does Mummy pop up in the crossover section?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T11:14:58-07:00","id":1106656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106653#post1106653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Mummy pop up in the crossover section?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. No woof, hunter or mummy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T11:24:53-07:00","id":1106659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106646#post1106646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're right that Requiem is consistent with what constitutes an Elder. So it's not specifically this book that I disagree with. It's just more relevant with this book. I just find those numbers to be quite underwhelming.<br /> <br /> I haven't played Masquerade, if that's what you're alluding to, but everyone in my group has, and I'm probably somewhat influenced by them since we've met several Elders in our campaign that have been in Torpor due to advanced BP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires become elders in Masquerade at 200 years, at least in the US. The European Camarilla regards vampires of at least 400 years of age to be elders.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T11:34:01-07:00","id":1106662,"title":"","content":"Okay, there's a few criticisms of the critique I have. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106617#post1106617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Side note - I'm still not understanding what the picture of the guy holding his bleeding arm, and the woman on the ground holding her head screaming, gun next to her. Page 28. Is that supposed to be overloaded senses? The Curse of Five coming into play?<br /> <br /> <b>Actually, I think it's misplaced-looks like feeding on an Inanamorta to me.</b><br /> <br /> And we get to the first part of the book's fluff I'm not liking. I feel like the covenant section is basically summed up as &quot;you get cults of personality, flavored by covenant philosophy.&quot; Or &quot;go off on your own.&quot; I don't feel there's much here to explore beyond &quot;trusted elders = leadership roles.&quot; And I also feel like we're dealing more with the 1e covenants rather than the expanded 2e. I loved the different flavors of the Circle we saw in Secrets, but here? Back to the pseud-wicca Mother-Maiden-Crone bits. No references to the Invictus as the Masquerade enforces, just as Establishment. Dynasty is listed under Invictus again, despite the core pushing it towards clan-based (Also - The reference to dynasty oath could use a page reference, or something, as I was getting it confused with the core book merit). Dynasties have nothing to do with covenant! If anything, it should have been under Clan! And that sidebar! Dynasties are already cross covenant by nature. Its utterly meaningless.<br /> <br /> <b>Someone should really tell that to the Covenants. About the only one that doesn't actually care is the Carthians, and they're <i>the Carthians</i>. The Sanctified and Acolytes have need of Blood Sympathy for rituals, the Defiant want to research &quot;genes&quot;, and the Invictus are literally a neo-monarchy-dynasty is kind of their thing, along with the Masquerade and their meritocracy (and the core mentioned the upper ranks are so practiced with it they don't have to care in their nightly life-it's a reflex to them).</b><br /> <br /> Cerberus pact feels like a variation on VII. Which might have been the intent - playable VII that doesn't tell you what the VII are. Its got its appeal, but I'm still not sure why we're going with elder-only, however. I don't feel anything elder-ish about the Pact.<br /> <br /> <b>Paranoia, hubris, the fact there's only three of them per hunting party...</b><br /> <br /> <b>III. The Long Solo</b><br /> We start with a small thing about why vampires prize memories and &quot;transcend history.&quot; Feel like there's references to how Ancient books talked about vampire history. Cool. Vampire elders want to make a mark on the world and not be forgotten. Okay. Ah, Flashback scenes. Now this is tasty. Not a fan of all the Masquerade-era &quot;vampires fear change&quot; leaking in, but ideas for going back in history is nice. Nothing immediately useful outside of an elder game, but solid ideas on what to focus on. I like structuring it on idfferent themes like love or intrigue or the Embrace. Nothing really stands out to me, but that's because I dont have an immediate need for it. I can see the definite value during future games, however.<br /> <br /> <b>Everyone fears change, and everyone wants progress. It's a human theme, not a Masquerade theme.</b><br /> <br /> <b>IV. What we Learned Along the Way</b><br /> Aww... first chapter title not related to music. Sadness. So, we have a section on 6+ attributes. Okay. I don't understand why its unique to elders, when its basically something that all vampires experince through disciplines. Wits made me feel like it was talking about an Auspex user. Strength and Stamina above 5 are common with disciplines, and they can't be turned off.<br /> <br /> <b>Because those are enhancements. For an elder who's embraced her superhuman potential, it's the baseline. And it's not something given to them directly by a superhuman power they have, an elder with Wits 6 is literally just that perceptive; she's Sherlock Holmes, able to explain someone's life story because she noticed a scratch on a cell phone.</b><br /> <br /> Scapegoat... just not a fan of the magical implications of being able to avoid derangements. You take derangements if you learn about something you did under frenzy later. Yet &quot;because magic&quot; you get to go crazy and do whatever without problem. Theban's Curse of Isolation has issues - putting aside things like forests or tombs as touchstones, but it doesn't touch on things like Impression, or if we're dealing with transfered feelings or anything. Very clunky. What happens when someone uses this against a True Friend touchstone? Or a faded touchstone? Orison of Voices is cool - you get to hear prayers directed to you. Not really worth a five dot ritual, especially when we have merits for regnants appearing in trouble. Cool, but should have been a merit with a Theban prerequisite. Sins of the Ancestors feels like it should be an Auspex power, and is of dubious use. Iconic, I suppose, but not something I see come up in play often, either for PCs or NPCs.<br /> <br /> <b>The problem with this is the very beginning; there's no such thing as derangements any more. Scapegoat is the Circle of the Crone's philosophy in miniature. Humanity is necessary, but more of an obstacle to transcendence; by storing it away, they can do the things that the Acolytes do if they've been pushed and know they don't need to worry about losing their minds to Wassail (as for the Scapegoat, screw mortals-who knows, their flagging Integrity may allow them to build something better than before). You misread Orison of Voices (it hears <i>every </i>conversation <i>in the world</i> where your name was mentioned, and gleans the context-it's probably the most OP Theban Sorcery power for anyone with any interest in politics), you can't do anything to a True Friend without player permission so that's a non-issue for any PC, and the questions Sins allow you to ask is <i>any </i>simple question-you get to interrogate a target's entire direct family, for any reason for a Vitae drop.</b><br /> <br /> Coil of the Quintessence. There's some implications here. 1) we can extend one of the three core coils by attaching a new Coil to a Mystery. 2) A coil built around territory control means we can have coils that do more than affect the vampire itself. Still a bit weak in terms of actual mechanics - Smother (and Cold of the Grave by extension) and Forever Mine are good. Everything else is questionable, imho.<br /> <br /> <b>It is incredibly useful for a Prince-you know freaking everything that happens, at least in general, and the very first dot allows you to be effectively omnipresent. You don't do anything in the Dragon's city and expect him to not notice.</b><br /> <br /> Dynasty Merits - So, Dynastic Progenitor can be cool. Flat dice bonus to discipline use, but sure. Oath of Dynasty... Dynasties are not made, nor confirmed, by Notories. You already share blood sympathy with everyone, because you're all part of the same clan to begin with! Talking with torpid members is already done via Speaker for the Silent. I'm sorry, but I feel like whomever wrote this section on Dynasties was stuck with the old Invictus book instead of how the actual merits work in 2e. I feel like this Oath of Dynasty was meant to be the book's Invictus Oath. But, it doesn't even lean towards that.<br /> <br /> <b>It never was; they explicitly said there's more than one Oath of Dynasty than Invictus ones, and even suggested them in a sidebar. It's just called that, because it's still an oath between elders.</b><br /> <br /> Touchstones get a bit of look at, but in another way - faux Touchstones that work differently. Its definitely an interesting take to reflect things, especially when combined with phantom touchstones. I'm pleased with tthe variety of touchstones presented in the book. The Halfway Port: Ghouls at least firmly establishes ghouls as potential touchstones, and not as human company. Discusses ghouls in an elder's life, though not in too much detail. Probably could have skipped this in favor of the half-damned book. The Death Barge: Revenants... I'm not sure what's going on here. &quot;There but for the Grace of God...&quot; Huh? Isn't that a draugr? Outcasts? They can be uplifted fairly easily, and wanted to by most cities, I imagine. Revenants are used to track sloppy feeders. Maybe serving as a touchstone? Wha? Given the next section on vampires, you can have other vampires a kind of faux touchstone... huh. I admit to skimming this part, as there's just too much to really focus on.<br /> <br /> <b>Revenants are the mirror that you can talk to; they're all Curse, no consolation, and as mentioned in the core, they have a huge prejudice against them that puts the lie to them being wanted. It's not rational; it still happens, and it's a huge problem that leads to many stories.</b><br /> <br /> [stuff about dragur I accidentally deleted]<br /> <br /> <b>Not socially. But the fluff is your friend-dragur are not lacking in cunning, they lurk in places where they have the advantage. The short-lived dragur are the one who can't find lairs; once they do, they tend to be quite happy to not threaten the Masquerade if only to help their hunts.</b><br /> <br /> Body of a Nation - tier 3 global threats for elders in the form of Danse Macabre Conspiracy?<br /> <br /> <b>That, and a quiet remark on shadow politics-the Body is a group that controls the American Government...in the name of the American Government. They formed up because they were all friends of Ben Franklin, and it's a tragedy they've been hijacked by something.</b><br /> <br /> Immortals:<br /> Deborah - basically, an immortal hunter, with a Compact/Conspiriacy based on her family, using psychic abilities.<br /> King Kitamba - another immortal hunter that may as well be a rogue ghoul with a slightly better time frame between feedings.<br /> Sons of Phobos - reprint from Blood Sorcery book, basically.<br /> <br /> <b>Except for the part where the Sons are completely different; they aren't Roman cultists blessed by the Strix, they're Greek sorcerers who have their unique type of blood magic altogether not unlike Cruac, but its own thing. They've also been buffed with more rituals and the ability to use Vampire Disciplines.</b><br /> <br /> Crossover section - notes on immortal mages (liches), long lived 'lings, and more. The only thing I'm going to mention is that no, Auras aren't how Auspex work anymore. Not really a fan of crossover, so skipping over.<br /> <br /> <b>Which is a fucking shame, as that is probably the best written section. Changeling blood causes the vampire to hallucinate being alive again, meaning a changeling blood doll is likely the powerful one in this relationship, as the changeling is likely quite capable of cutting the flow whenever he feels like it. And it gets more interesting from there, very respectful and conscious of all game lines.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> All in all, I can't say I'm impressed with this chapter. Feels like its just taking existing things and putting more stats on them. Same things as the neonate, just hits harder.<br /> <br /> <b>VII In Conclusion</b><br /> <br /> So. There you go. Basically, we have some very good ideas that go into the thought process of being an elder, how to build up history, some really good story hooks, new Touchstone ideas, and the occasional devotion worth having.<br /> <br /> If youw ant to do an elder game and need help getting into the mindset, good book to get. If you want it for the mechanics or antagonists? I suggest checking elsewhere.<br /> <br /> <b>Actually, it's also good if you want elder antagonists, it's a vital insight to how they think.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T11:47:23-07:00","id":1106667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106547#post1106547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forvo.com/word/la/praestantia/\" target=\"_blank\">https://forvo.com/word/la/praestantia/</a></div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T11:49:22-07:00","id":1106669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106662#post1106662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, there's a few criticisms of the critique I have.</div> </div> </div> </div>..... <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T12:18:05-07:00","id":1106684,"title":"","content":"So mechanics.<br /> <br /> - Skills at 6+<br /> These are a welcome addition to the game. If anything, I wish it was a mechanic that was played with more.<br /> <br /> - Devotions<br /> Annuls of Death is good, fluffy and a cheap expansion to Auspex 3. The concepts that want it will love it.<br /> <br /> Bones of the Mountain - Follows the concept of &quot;so long as a vamp jemmorages blood, they win combat.&quot; It's pretty powerful, and I like it. Personally I don't think this will ever be worth the exp as a PC (there are other uses of your exp that are more efficient out to 200-300xp), but its a neat out of context threat for your fighter to face.<br /> <br /> Celebrity - This is the first power that seems on a whole different tier of power. Use it on your Ghoul, and you suddenly have a soirce of nigh unlimited Allies, Fame, Herd, Retainer, Staff and Status, with the downside that you are popular. Use with Alternate Identity.<br /> <br /> Consumption - Pretty great, if niche devotion. Instantly enslaving mortals decinately has its uses, as does possessing people from over the phone.<br /> <br /> Crush of Years - <br /> <br /> Legion - Niche, but powerful. Has that whole master of the land field. I wish it didnt require Auspex, since its very Gangrel and Ventrue themed.<br /> <br /> Malignant Smog - Interesting thematically. Mechanically it's pretty powerful (hello Immobilize and Stun). We need to know the Potency of the poison you turn in to, if applicable. Sadly, I feel like most people will pass the roll to ignore the condition. Also! Good example of using Blood Potency in mechamics to make the devotion more appealing to elders. I don't know what happens if someone is affected every 0 turns, which is technically possible.<br /> <br /> Pass into Yesteryear - Epic, thematically and mechanically. Its a blessing, a &quot;blessing&quot; and a curse to pass out to people.<br /> <br /> Praternatural Instinct - They are *really* pushing Mekhet as being masters of defense. Its great, but requires so much Auspex.<br /> <br /> Spontanious Ignition - This is lulz, and likely to set everything on fire. Doing things with Fire is always tricky, but I feel this devotion does it as respectfully as possible. I do feel that this is a very &quot;why you should fear elders&quot; power. Surviving their own ignition, however...<br /> <br /> Unbridled Force - Epic, iconic, perfect. Vampire telekonesis is a go.<br /> <br /> Overall - These Devotions are pretty well written, but I'm not sure if they feel particularly like Elder exclusive things. It never feels like the Elder has transcended or broken through. Imo, Elders should be borderline out of context problems for those of lesser blood. This just feels like some nice Devotions.<br /> <br /> Exceptions are Spontanious Ignition, Unbridled Force, Legion, and maybe Bones of the Mountain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T12:30:17-07:00","id":1106692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106684#post1106684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Skills at 6+<br /> These are a welcome addition to the game. If anything, I wish it was a mechanic that was played with more.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a new thing. BP governs Attribute and Skill Maximum in the core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T12:31:41-07:00","id":1106693,"title":"","content":"Blood Sorcery<br /> The fluff section is nice. Doubling the costs is fluffy!<br /> <br /> The rituals themselves are... meh. <br /> Manananggal's Working - Its nice, and fluffy, and useful... but is it really an elder power?<br /> <br /> Gwydion's Curse is obviously meant to be used with Madrigora Garden (which will hopefully get errata so it works). It works off Potency, which is a terrible mechanic, so you wont be animating anything of size. The dicepool is meh, but its &quot;free&quot; I guess. The plants dont seem to be under the ritualist's control, so apparently they are in danger too? If the plants were under the kindred's control and it affected a meaningful area it would be worth it. I want to lile this, but the mechanics don't back it up.<br /> <br /> Scapegoat feels expensive for what it does. I also don't like avoiding detatchments as being a thing Cruac can do, even like this.<br /> <br /> Curse of Isolation - This is interesting, if expensive. I wish it had more oomph for its exp cost, amd I wish the mechanics went into what stealing a touchstone actually meant.<br /> <br /> Orison of Voices - Epic and appropriate. This is an elder power.<br /> <br /> Sins of the Ancestors - This is a remarkably open-ended power with no guidance on the scope of questions that can be asked. I kind of like it as an elder power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T12:53:11-07:00","id":1106702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106669#post1106669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">..... <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, it's not a bad review. I just caught a few things where I thought you misread things. Might as well point out my own opinion in the process, where it differs from yours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T12:58:20-07:00","id":1106704,"title":"","content":"Mysteries of the Dragon<br /> <br /> Quintessence<br /> 1 - Fluffy, great, estabmishes an Elder-ish hold over a domain.<br /> 2 - This power is gold, so long as you can phrase what you're doing as being related to feeding.<br /> 3 - This one is pretty out of left field. I wish it was tied more to the themes of the coil, maybe also mitigating environmental penalties.<br /> 4 - ... Strangely, I think this one lets you sleep in sunlight. Its honestly kind of meh for what it is, but thats because I don't think much of those merits.<br /> 5 - Nice but doesn't feel capstone-y? <br /> <br /> I feel like the coil just shrugs about its own themes and fluff. I'd like a stronger thematic focus.<br /> <br /> Both scales are great benefits that the Ordo Dracul can spread over a domain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T15:00:56-07:00","id":1106748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106704#post1106704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mysteries of the Dragon<br /> <br /> Quintessence<br /> 1 - Fluffy, great, estabmishes an Elder-ish hold over a domain.<br /> 2 - This power is gold, so long as you can phrase what you're doing as being related to feeding.<br /> 3 - This one is pretty out of left field. I wish it was tied more to the themes of the coil, maybe also mitigating environmental penalties.<br /> 4 - ... Strangely, I think this one lets you sleep in sunlight. Its honestly kind of meh for what it is, but thats because I don't think much of those merits.<br /> 5 - Nice but doesn't feel capstone-y?<br /> <br /> I feel like the coil just shrugs about its own themes and fluff. I'd like a stronger thematic focus.<br /> <br /> Both scales are great benefits that the Ordo Dracul can spread over a domain.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree there. Actually I think switching 5 to 3 and replacing 5 with something more dramatic would work wonders.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106692#post1106692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not a new thing. BP governs Attribute and Skill Maximum in the core book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think he meant the mechanics for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T15:35:04-07:00","id":1106756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orzhov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106656#post1106656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. No woof, hunter or mummy</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty huge miss. Where else would Mummies fit if not in the elders book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T16:22:05-07:00","id":1106766,"title":"","content":"Sorry Lex, Elders don't want to talk about mummies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T16:44:31-07:00","id":1106773,"title":"","content":"Is there any reason why the Invictus elders didn't receive any special Oaths, or was the Oath of Dynasty supposed to be their new toy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T16:54:51-07:00","id":1106779,"title":"","content":"I would think a prerequisite for being an Elder is learning to avoid Mummies.<br /> <br /> I liked the review and the critique, the more information the better to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T17:15:42-07:00","id":1106791,"title":"","content":"I liked many of the devotions, I liked the &quot;Lost&quot; clans, I liked some of the blood sorcery rituals, some of the conditions, liked the Elder Character generation rules. <br /> <br /> I disliked the merits, would take maybe Mother Goddess' Altar or Married nothing else interests me, and even those two are unlikely. I also don't like scapegoat.<br /> <br /> Over all aside from the Elder Character &quot;template&quot; most things don't feel Elder Epic.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of using the MCI merit for groups/factions within covenants, like I could see using the MCI merit to create various Knightly Orders with different agendas and a Belial Cult within Lancea Sanctum. <br /> <br /> The fiction is great.<br /> <br /> Still fun book.<br /> <br /> I think to get the, most out if this book you'll want secrets of the covenants. <br /> <br /> Lamia and Emupria we're awesome ideas, unfortunately they are just another two clans of vampires, with no Covenants. They officially aren't, Kindred I think, just mechanically,just like them. They needed a cool special power each to make them pop.<br /> <br /> Debrah was awesome, Buffy meets Xena warrior princess.<br /> <br /> Sons of Pheobes are neat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 06-22-2017, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T19:51:54-07:00","id":1106839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106756#post1106756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a pretty huge miss. Where else would Mummies fit if not in the elders book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again Mummy is the red-headed step-child. I feel like many authors aren't familiar with it, not having read it even, and thus omit it. I've been anticipating this book for a long time and not just for word count on mummies, but it's still a disappointment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T22:15:15-07:00","id":1106879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106839#post1106839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again Mummy is the red-headed step-child. I feel like many authors aren't familiar with it, not having read it even, and thus omit it. I've been anticipating this book for a long time and not just for word count on mummies, but it's still a disappointment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as many of us have had a chance to work on it, sadly. That being said, and I know it's still disappointing, I would expect there's going to be a <i>lot </i>of Mummy / Elder Kindred discussion in The Crossover Chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T00:47:12-07:00","id":1106912,"title":"","content":"I think crossover with mummy when they in turn fall either into torpor or asleep(no idea what is mummy term) and can communicate only via written messages they leave for each other would be hilarious. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T04:16:58-07:00","id":1106951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1106879#post1106879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not as many of us have had a chance to work on it, sadly. That being said, and I know it's still disappointing, I would expect there's going to be a <i>lot </i>of Mummy / Elder Kindred discussion in The Crossover Chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>There will indeed be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T12:46:10-07:00","id":1107092,"title":"","content":"So... Anyone else confused by the decision to give Julii Vigor instead of Animalism? I don't really get it. Commanding animals as well as people seemed very thematic, and it created that ambiguity of origin between the Julii, Ventrue, and Gangrel since they were all so similar. I just don't see how Vigor fits in...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T13:02:51-07:00","id":1107097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107092#post1107092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... Anyone else confused by the decision to give Julii Vigor instead of Animalism? I don't really get it. Commanding animals as well as people seemed very thematic, and it created that ambiguity of origin between the Julii, Ventrue, and Gangrel since they were all so similar. I just don't see how Vigor fits in...</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda agree with this. If they wanted to make things bit more confusing they could drop Majesty(fits better imho)on this guys. Also the clan curse is kinda ech. It relies on external factors and can either cripple you or be nonissue depanding on the game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T13:33:12-07:00","id":1107105,"title":"","content":"I'm operating entirely on Second-Hand knowledge here, but the Requiem 2E Core write-up on the Julii seems pretty emphatic that these Kindred were a clan to be reckoned with. Vigor, (especially coupled with Resilience) plays into the theme of Unstoppable Force more than Animalism (which better plays into the theme of Canny Manipulator).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T14:15:58-07:00","id":1107119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107092#post1107092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... Anyone else confused by the decision to give Julii Vigor instead of Animalism? I don't really get it. Commanding animals as well as people seemed very thematic, and it created that ambiguity of origin between the Julii, Ventrue, and Gangrel since they were all so similar. I just don't see how Vigor fits in...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree exactly (in the sense that I think your criticism is totally valid, but I don't ascribe to it), but I adore the change. I always wanted them to be just a <i>little </i>more different. I like the idea that they're Warriors and Emperors. They're not predators like the Gangrel, or just power mongers like the Ventrue. They're conquerors, which is very Roman: <i>Veni, vidi, vici</i>. I also just like the double barrel of Resilience/Vigor. Makes them a nice contrast to the Daeva.<br /> <br /> It also helps that, while Second Edition Animalism is <i>fantastic</i>, it's never been my favourite Discipline.<br /> <br /> Or, at least, that's my elevator pitch; I still think your fan version of Second Ed. Julii was the best of a wide field <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: It also fits into that conceit in RfR (and this probably wasn't intentional but I like this interpretation) that the Julii don't see their abilities as &quot;supernatural&quot;; it's just that they're <i>Roman</i>. I tell people what to do and they do it. I crush my enemies with my bare fists. No barbarian can strike me down. Animalism in Second Edition is a lot more overtly supernatural.<br /> <br /> Edit edit: And yeah, it does muddy the canon waters a bit, but it kind of puts lie to the Ventrue and their claims of a storied past. I've always liked the idea that they're a bunch of inbred Gangrel who stole the &quot;Lordly Words&quot; from the Julii.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 06-23-2017, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T15:27:35-07:00","id":1107137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107119#post1107119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't disagree exactly (in the sense that I think your criticism is totally valid, but I don't ascribe to it), but I adore the change. I always wanted them to be just a <i>little </i>more different. I like the idea that they're Warriors and Emperors. They're not predators like the Gangrel, or just power mongers like the Ventrue. They're conquerors, which is very Roman: <i>Veni, vidi, vici</i>. I also just like the double barrel of Resilience/Vigor. Makes them a nice contrast to the Daeva.<br /> <br /> It also helps that, while Second Edition Animalism is <i>fantastic</i>, it's never been my favourite Discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... I dunno, I think command is a better fit than brute force. I get not liking Animalism, but I would sooner replace it with Majesty, although I wouldn't do that because it's the Daeva signature discipline. And I get the appeal of Vigor but I would sooner replace Resilience with it, although I wouldn't do that either because as mentioned before I like how the Ventrue spread makes them very close to both Ventrue and Gangrel. I lways thought of the three as a triumvirate that represented how blurry the lines of Clan can be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107119#post1107119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, at least, that's my elevator pitch; I still think your fan version of Second Ed. Julii was the best of a wide field <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I'll probably use the canon version next time I run Rome, but I'm glad my stop gap solution was well-liked.<br /> <br /> (edit: though I'll probably keep my Detached Curse as their Bane and make the Strigid Curse or something like it their Elder Bane. Weakness to Strix possession is appropriate for the Julii, but doesn't seem like it would impact play as much as the other Clan Banes do.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107119#post1107119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: It also fits into that conceit in RfR (and this probably wasn't intentional but I like this interpretation) that the Julii don't see their abilities as &quot;supernatural&quot;; it's just that they're <i>Roman</i>. I tell people what to do and they do it. I crush my enemies with my bare fists. No barbarian can strike me down. Animalism in Second Edition is a lot more overtly supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, <i>that</i> sold me. I always liked that interpretation (so much so in fact that I carry it over into how Disiplines are viewed in my modern games). One of the most challenging parts of writing my Julii treatment was trying to make Animalism sound convincingly natural. I had to really focus on it as an extension of the obedience thing and downplay the more overt aspects like raising undead familiars. So ok, if Vigor instead of Animalism makes that pill easier to swallow, it's a worthwhile tradeoff for them being less directly connected with Ventrue and Gangrel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107119#post1107119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit edit: And yeah, it does muddy the canon waters a bit, but it kind of puts lie to the Ventrue and their claims of a storied past. I've always liked the idea that they're a bunch of inbred Gangrel who stole the &quot;Lordly Words&quot; from the Julii.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my preferred interpretation as well, but I liked that Ventrue as direct successors to Julii was also a plausible interpretation, even if it was a lie in my head canon. While you've convinced me the change is worth the sacrifice, I do feel something is lost in making it more transparently untrue that Ventrue are direct successors of the Julii.<br /> <br /> On the plus side, I know what 4th Discipline to give my Macellarius update now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-23-2017, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T18:05:39-07:00","id":1107164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107137#post1107137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks! I'll probably use the canon version next time I run Rome, but I'm glad my stop gap solution was well-liked.<br /> <br /> (edit: though I'll probably keep my Detached Curse as their Bane and make the Strigid Curse or something like it their Elder Bane. Weakness to Strix possession is appropriate for the Julii, but doesn't seem like it would impact play as much as the other Clan Banes do.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooo, I like that idea! I'm going to toss your Julii in the Booklist thread so that others can use it. I did find myself missing the fact that the Lost Clans didn't have Elder Banes, so that is a perfect fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T18:43:16-07:00","id":1107171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107164#post1107164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooo, I like that idea! I'm going to toss your Julii in the Booklist thread so that others can use it. I did find myself missing the fact that the Lost Clans didn't have Elder Banes, so that is a perfect fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much! For the Akhud, I'd make the permanent diablerie stains their Elder Bane instead of attaching them to Prestantia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-23-2017, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T21:47:22-07:00","id":1107206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107119#post1107119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Edit edit: And yeah, it does muddy the canon waters a bit, but it kind of puts lie to the Ventrue and their claims of a storied past. I've always liked the idea that they're a bunch of inbred Gangrel who stole the &quot;Lordly Words&quot; from the Julii.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107137#post1107137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was my preferred interpretation as well, but I liked that Ventrue as direct successors to Julii was also a plausible interpretation, even if it was a lie in my head canon. While you've convinced me the change is worth the sacrifice, I do feel something is lost in making it more transparently untrue that Ventrue are direct successors of the Julii.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if the shift from animalism to vigor makes the statement that the Ventrue were descended from the Julii any less true. I think the difference between having a Clan Discipline and having a common discipline is significant, and because of that it's still much more likely that the Ventrue were related to the Julii than to the Gangrel. On the other hand, the fact that they are now as different from the Julii as they are from the Gangrel technically could be a great basis of debate. Or a great way to say they are related to both. &quot;The noble clan Julii had descendents that fell from the grace of from, sullying their blood with the savages&quot; is just as likely an option as &quot;Savages stole the words of power from the Julii&quot; no? :P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T03:49:40-07:00","id":1107277,"title":"","content":"Why are the elders made with this book such a joke? 25-35 Exp for most elders and they are described as vastly superior to neonates is just sad. Really that is just a few dots above starting neonates. And the arcs you can buy, you cant afford and they are severly lacking in disciplines cus non of them buys you any dot there. <br /> Really the age table should go. If its an elder just see on the table, if its a rank elder or a mover and shaker and choose the appropriate exp and let the age be a part of the background not really bonud to exp. <br /> But why are pc elders worthless? Why have a book about playing them when they cant even be close to how they are described?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","user":"Poseur","date":". 06-24-2017, 06:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T04:36:27-07:00","id":1107285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107277#post1107277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are the elders made with this book such a joke? 25-35 Exp for most elders and they are described as vastly superior to neonates is just sad. Really that is just a few dots above starting neonates. And the arcs you can buy, you cant afford and they are severly lacking in disciplines cus non of them buys you any dot there.<br /> Really the age table should go. If its an elder just see on the table, if its a rank elder or a mover and shaker and choose the appropriate exp and let the age be a part of the background not really bonud to exp.<br /> But why are pc elders worthless? Why have a book about playing them when they cant even be close to how they are described?</div> </div> </div> </div>The XP is as low as it is because it's not retconning what was said in VtR 2e core book. The age table is identical to the numbers given back in Blood and Smoke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T05:04:50-07:00","id":1107287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107285#post1107285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The XP is as low as it is because it's not retconning what was said in VtR 2e core book. The age table is identical to the numbers given back in Blood and Smoke.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two wrongs dosnt make one right. <br /> Its just bad your fiction dosnt even closely hold up to the rules. <br /> And maybe there was a age-table in blood and smoke but in ny 2ed ut sure dosnt say anything about age in that exp table. Mover and shaker is a describtion , same with Urban legend, not an age group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","user":"Poseur","date":".  Spelling. Auto correct in swedish is a joy. 06-24-2017, 08:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T07:17:59-07:00","id":1107302,"title":"","content":"They also get blood potency 5 by default, so that's an extra 20 experiences right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T07:27:04-07:00","id":1107304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107302#post1107302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They also get blood potency 5 by default, so that's an extra 20 experiences right there.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not exactly an advantage. It means they start the game requiring kindred blood to feed which means they also have to purchase merits enabling them to feed off other things if they're available in the setting or purchasing powers to enable them to obviate the blood bond, which means they have to buy the attendant pre-requisites for that (covenant status, multiple sorcery ranks, scales etc.) or else quickly end up blood bound to someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T07:29:55-07:00","id":1107308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107304#post1107304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not exactly an advantage. It means they start the game requiring kindred blood to feed which means they also have to purchase merits enabling them to feed off other things if they're available in the setting or purchasing powers to enable them to obviate the blood bond, which means they have to buy the attendant pre-requisites for that (covenant status, multiple sorcery ranks, scales etc.) or else quickly end up blood bound to someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kindred blood is required at 6","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T07:35:16-07:00","id":1107310,"title":"","content":"So the Julii now have Vigor, and the Akhud don't have any connection to Shaddad? Well, it seems like I'll have to make few changes for my Akhud version and my Mumvuri (as they also have the same Discipline spread as the Julii have right now, not to mention the weird way they interact with their own &quot;strix&quot;).<br /> <br /> I have only gave the book a shallow look right now, but I'm a bit disappointed that the Lamia and Empusa writetup seems a bit shallow- but the concept of Elder Banes and the Elder mechanics seems really interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T08:11:06-07:00","id":1107318,"title":"","content":"Just because Shaddad wasn't mentioned here doesn't necessarily mean the Akhud don't have any connection to him any more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T08:26:48-07:00","id":1107321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107318#post1107318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because Shaddad wasn't mentioned here doesn't necessarily mean the Akhud don't have any connection to him any more.</div> </div> </div> </div>well, it looked like that every mention of the Akhud in 2E claims them to be the vampires which caused the destruction of the Five Cities in the original writeup, instead of the descendants of the mortal survivors. I'm not saying that Shaddad does not exist anymore in the setting- only that it looks like 2E distance itself from him and the original version. On the other hand, I did only gave a brief look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T08:41:41-07:00","id":1107324,"title":"","content":"One of the few things that I am disappointed about in the book is the lack of pictures for the sample Elder Kindred. I know not every NPC gets a picture, but the whole section is just absent of character portraits <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Besides that - content wise it's a good read so far; I haven't gone through all of it yet - but I've enjoyed what I have read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T08:57:16-07:00","id":1107330,"title":"","content":"Related to that, do lost clans have images?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T09:23:44-07:00","id":1107335,"title":"","content":"The Pijavica does. It was posted in the Monday Meeting blog a while back. If you mean the symbols, then not as far as I can tell, though Rome might have Julii symbols and VII has the Akhud.<br /> <br /> They sort of look like normal people. Hollow Mekhet like Mekhet, but without a reflection. I suppose it would have been nice to see the 'blob' form of a Pijavica. There might be an image for it I haven't seen but, really, it's a pool of blood and vitae so not too hard to imagine.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/05/Araya-Thousand-Years-of-Night.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> That's Vlastislav, the last Pijavica.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107277#post1107277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are the elders made with this book such a joke? 25-35 Exp for most elders and they are described as vastly superior to neonates is just sad. Really that is just a few dots above starting neonates. And the arcs you can buy, you cant afford and they are severly lacking in disciplines cus non of them buys you any dot there.<br /> Really the age table should go. If its an elder just see on the table, if its a rank elder or a mover and shaker and choose the appropriate exp and let the age be a part of the background not really bonud to exp.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's 25-35 Experiences more than a neonate. That's a good amount, especially considering how cheap everything is in second edition. You can get six Attributes and a Merit with just 25 Experiences, that's a Rank Elder, someone who's just an Elder due to their age. You can get 17 Skills with 35.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-24-2017, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T09:53:26-07:00","id":1107340,"title":"","content":"Well I might be ridiculous but I give my vamps 1 exp per year of unlife so I admit rules in the book cracked me up","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T09:55:52-07:00","id":1107341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orzhov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107340#post1107340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I might be ridiculous but I give my vamps 1 exp per year of unlife so I admit rules in the book cracked me up</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but everything in the book seems to make you laugh so that's not new. Just remember if you see something erroneous to put it in the errata thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","va