ps://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107485#post1107485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah I'm just being a pessimist. They've said they still exist, and there's the rite in the Secrets of the Covenants. Seems like with second edition what you'd do is take the covenants and turn them on their head, then have the 'true' Brood as dark manipulators and explorers of the greater darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah I can see Belials Brood being a Lancea Sanctum conspiracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T19:23:26-07:00","id":1107491,"title":"","content":"Anyone else see the Cerebrus Pact being mostly made up of Julii, no one else has the same level of motivation against the Strix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T19:28:02-07:00","id":1107492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107383#post1107383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had hoped that the XP totals for elders in this book would be a bit more elderlike.<br /> <br /> Not a big deal, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You realize that, in the core VtR book, an Elder is just 150 years old or more and is given an XP value of 25, yes? They aren't quite as extreme as some people seem to have expected.<br /> <br /> I think some people went into the Elder book expecting Ancients.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T20:02:24-07:00","id":1107495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107492#post1107492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You realize that, in the core VtR book, an Elder is just 150 years old or more and is given an XP value of 25, yes? They aren't quite as extreme as some people seem to have expected.<br /> <br /> I think some people went into the Elder book expecting Ancients.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do realize that, and I disagree with the xp totals given. 100 experiences for a Methuselah?<br /> <br /> People don't need to get defensive about someone not liking the rules as they're written. It's fine to not like them, and it's fine to find solutions for that. Not everyone has the same criteria for everything.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T20:40:17-07:00","id":1107503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107495#post1107495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People don't need to get defensive about someone not liking the rules as they're written. It's fine to not like them, and it's fine to find solutions for that. Not everyone has the same criteria for everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in this case its less that people do or do not like them than they feel elders are something different compared to how they've been portrayed in the material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T21:48:37-07:00","id":1107510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107503#post1107503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think in this case its less that people do or do not like them than they feel elders are something different compared to how they've been portrayed in the material.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like the rules as they are written because I feel elders are something different compared to how they're portrayed in the rules. Not a difference in <i>kind,</i> but rather a difference of <i>magnitude</i>.<br /> <br /> So it's not a matter of one thing or the other.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T22:04:09-07:00","id":1107512,"title":"","content":"At first I wasn't sure what to think about the experience points either, but I've slowly come around to it. Part of the reason it isn't impressive at first glance is because typically in a game we'll see the PCs get to around 30xp or more, and I guess it's supposed to be taken that the PCs just get into more trouble than most young Kindred; thus more experience means more experience. I've partially come around to the suggested amounts because Elders (probably) don't spend the entirety of their requiem awake, and more than likely some time was spent in torpor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T01:17:28-07:00","id":1107571,"title":"","content":"The only thing I felt missing was the use of Advanced and Epic Merits. I figured Elders would be the perfect chance to explore what those could be in a more social venue, and guessed that the applicatons of 6+ skills and attributes would be better based on merits that escalated as the character did.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I loved it in terms of fluff and setting. It really sold me on the idea of actually playing Elder Vampiires rather than having them as a hazard you dealt with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T07:02:00-07:00","id":1107623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107571#post1107571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing I felt missing was the use of Advanced and Epic Merits. I figured Elders would be the perfect chance to explore what those could be in a more social venue, and guessed that the applicatons of 6+ skills and attributes would be better based on merits that escalated as the character did.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I loved it in terms of fluff and setting. It really sold me on the idea of actually playing Elder Vampiires rather than having them as a hazard you dealt with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I felt the same way about Advanced and Epic merits, I was actually just talking about that with someone the other day. Definitely would've made sense, the thematics of typically mundane talents drawn to unnatural levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T16:32:13-07:00","id":1107793,"title":"","content":"Slightly off the flow of the topic, but I was thinking about the new Julii Bane and how much I like it. I think the Strix parts are pretty obvious, but I really like the extra dagger in their backs about it applying to all ephemeral beings. Romans were obsessed with ancestor worship: they held festivals in honor of their dead family members, and made sacrifices to malevolent ghosts to keep them off their backs. Nobility publicly venerated their departed loved ones with inscriptions and statues, and Roman emperors were elevated into godhood upon death.<br /> <br /> A low Humanity Julii is a superstitious monster. She knows the dead and the gods are always watching (and judging), and she makes sure she never crosses them. Even if she doesn't give a shit about the Vaticinators and their &quot;prophecies&quot;, she goes to every damn augury because that's what you <i>do.</i><br /> <br /> It also plays really well into that self-deceiving invincibility the Julii see in themselves. Young Julii look at the other Kindred with their &quot;banes&quot; and pity them. Julii have no weaknesses; the foreign clans are corrupt and twisted. Old Julii know better: they know that this is the weight of destiny. Only a Roman could be so blessed by his righteous ancestors, and the great patron gods of Rome. It's not a burden: it's responsibility. The Julii know obedience to their patrons, nothing more.<br /> <br /> Of course, a few Julii know the truth, but their havens are little but ash, filled with fragments of coal-black feathers<br /> <br /> (This isn't any attempt to argue against people who don't care for it, this is just what I found neat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T16:54:13-07:00","id":1107806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107793#post1107793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (This isn't any attempt to argue against people who don't care for it, this is just what I found neat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, I heard of it only by people talking about it here and yet I can already agree that's quite neat!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T17:01:14-07:00","id":1107809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107793#post1107793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slightly off the flow of the topic, but I was thinking about the new Julii Bane and how much I like it. I think the Strix parts are pretty obvious, but I really like the extra dagger in their backs about it applying to all ephemeral beings. Romans were obsessed with ancestor worship: they held festivals in honor of their dead family members, and made sacrifices to malevolent ghosts to keep them off their backs. Nobility publicly venerated their departed loved ones with inscriptions and statues, and Roman emperors were elevated into godhood upon death.<br /> <br /> A low Humanity Julii is a superstitious monster. She knows the dead and the gods are always watching (and judging), and she makes sure she never crosses them. Even if she doesn't give a shit about the Vaticinators and their &amp;quot;prophecies&amp;quot;, she goes to every damn augury because that's what you <i>do.</i><br /> <br /> It also plays really well into that self-deceiving invincibility the Julii see in themselves. Young Julii look at the other Kindred with their &amp;quot;banes&amp;quot; and pity them. Julii have no weaknesses; the foreign clans are corrupt and twisted. Old Julii know better: they know that this is the weight of destiny. Only a Roman could be so blessed by his righteous ancestors, and the great patron gods of Rome. It's not a burden: it's responsibility. The Julii know obedience to their patrons, nothing more.<br /> <br /> Of course, a few Julii know the truth, but their havens are little but ash, filled with fragments of coal-black feathers<br /> <br /> (This isn't any attempt to argue against people who don't care for it, this is just what I found neat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div> It also makes Julii interesting for crossovers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T17:57:23-07:00","id":1107827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107489#post1107489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Imperial Mysteries for Awakening also had some suggested mechanics for attributes and skills at 6+.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For those who are interested, here's the very small section in Imperial Mysteries on the subject and system for attributes and skills at 6+<br /> <br /> ***[Mods: If I posted too much material, kindly delete. Thank you.]<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Storytelling Transhuman Ability<br /> <br /> How do you portray someone with Intelligence 7 or<br /> Persuasion 8? Minor archmasters may possess one or two<br /> 6-dot Attributes and Skills, putting them on par with the<br /> most gifted Sleepers who ever lived, but at 7 or 8 dots, traits<br /> approach levels the real world has never seen.<br /> <br /> Intellectual abilities are particularly challenging because<br /> they affect characters\u2019 ability to predict events and uncover<br /> information. If this becomes a question, cheat \u2014 assume<br /> transhuman intellects guess and compensate for circumstances<br /> that would normally only be known to the Storyteller,<br /> or plans executed by player controlled or Storyteller<br /> characters. If you give this privilege to Storyteller characters,<br /> players\u2019 transhumans deserve the same privileges. Furthermore,<br /> you should make it clear at the outset that these<br /> benefi ts are available, and impose reasonable limits.<br /> <br /> One approach to the challenge is to look at real situations<br /> that enhance natural abilities. A hyper-intelligent<br /> archmage possesses an internal \u201csearch engine\u201d that allows<br /> her to exploit her memories faster and more effectively,<br /> never gets her math wrong, and can fi nd patterns in extremely<br /> large data sets. Sleepers react to a Seeker with<br /> a Presence of 7 as if she was a celebrity, with the same<br /> degree of distraction and obsession. Characters with<br /> transhuman Physical Stamina scores recover from illness<br /> and injury as if they were under skilled medical care, even<br /> if they\u2019re alone in the wild. Characters with more than<br /> human Skills might be able to use them without normal<br /> tools, or possess an unusual level of focus and confi dence<br /> in stressful situations.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s important to note that traits in the Storytelling<br /> System do not necessarily match casual uses of the same<br /> words. For example, we may think that high intelligence<br /> correlates with the ability to predict and shape political<br /> institutions, but much of that \u201csocial\u201d intelligence is a<br /> better fi t for the Manipulation Attribute.<br /> <br /> Optional System: Reversal Points<br /> <br /> If you like, you might give hyper-competent characters<br /> possess \u201creversal points\u201d to represent superior insight and<br /> preparation. Each reversal point allows a player to retroactively<br /> declare a basic (1 point \u2013 bodyguards were shadowing<br /> you in case of attack), moderate (2 points \u2013 your countersniper<br /> shoots the sniper), complex (3 points \u2013 \u201cMy spy<br /> network knew about this weeks ago\u201d) preparation to deal<br /> with an event that has just been revealed in play, such as a<br /> betrayal or unexpected encounter.<br /> <br /> Your character possesses one reversal point for each dot<br /> in an Attribute or Skill above 5, and may only spend points<br /> when the situation would apply both to the linked Trait and<br /> the declared preparation. You may also spend points to nullify<br /> other characters\u2019 reversal points on a 1 for 1 basis.<br /> <br /> Your character recovers all reversal points at the start of<br /> each game chapter. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T02:12:23-07:00","id":1107948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1107495#post1107495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do realize that, and I disagree with the xp totals given. 100 experiences for a Methuselah?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's more what they called the levels of experience? The two Methuselah's they have in this book have 200+ XP (I think I counted one of them to ~300)? Maybe if they'd said that 25 xp is &quot;new elder&quot;, 35 is average, 50 is a &quot;mover and shaker&quot; and 100 is an &quot;urban legend&quot;, it would feel better. Or mabye even &quot;Urban Legend&quot; for 100 sounds a bit much. And leave the ancient monster off the scale altogether.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, I sort of felt like there was some ... epicness ... missing from the Elders' actual abilities. Like, maybe having abilities with 6+ dots should come with extra perks, aside from dice. Skills had some of that. I really liked the fluff that described high level abilities, but I guess maybe I wanted something mechanical as well.<br /> <br /> And I guess I wanted some more examples of powerful devotions. The ones that exist seem good enough. But I thought there'd be ... more.<br /> <br /> I really liked the theme of the book, though, and the descriptions were really great. I mostly felt that the mechanics didn't always hold up to the fluff. That's my spontaneous impression at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11756-razikale","name":"Razikale","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T12:45:10-07:00","id":1108111,"title":"","content":"Utukku seem to be a lost clan. Is this a new reference? I don't remember seeing it before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T12:53:15-07:00","id":1108115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1108111#post1108111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Utukku seem to be a lost clan. Is this a new reference? I don't remember seeing it before.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Utukku\" target=\"_blank\">Sort of.</a> Might be an Edimmu. There's probably a lot of 'lost clans' scattered throughout time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T13:21:59-07:00","id":1108124,"title":"","content":"On the subject of starting experience values, I think they look so low because they're meant to be for starting characters. 100 is definitely low for a Methuselah, as evidenced by the NPCs with over twice that much. But then, 0 is honestly pretty low for an adult human, let alone one who's been a vampire long enough to join a Covenant. I think they low-ball starting exp values so characters have room to grow over the course of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T13:29:08-07:00","id":1108127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1108124#post1108124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of starting experience values, I think they look so low because they're meant to be for starting characters. 100 is definitely low for a Methuselah, as evidenced by the NPCs with over twice that much. But then, 0 is honestly pretty low for an adult human, let alone one who's been a vampire long enough to join a Covenant. I think they low-ball starting exp values so characters have room to grow over the course of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, Zero xp is more teenager Innocents build, realistically speaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T15:08:31-07:00","id":1108163,"title":"","content":"I disagree. I think people underestimate a starting character's competence. Two dots in a skill is &quot;professional&quot; quality according to the book. How many skills is the average adult good enough at to do it professionally?<br /> <br /> Two dots in an attribute is &quot;average.&quot; How many adults that you know in real life do you think have 3s or 4s in an attribute?<br /> <br /> I think a starting character is actually pretty hyper-competent in CofD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T15:27:36-07:00","id":1108167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1108115#post1108115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Utukku\" target=\"_blank\">Sort of.</a> Might be an Edimmu. There's probably a lot of 'lost clans' scattered throughout time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Book mentioned Utukku of Ur a few times but one was when talking about lost clans and it was in the list with the others then. I think the suggestion was made that the number of lost clans would not be small. It seemed like the &quot;blood pikachu clan&quot; (forgot spelling and don't feel like looking it up) was teased before an official version was delivered. Maybe there will be some new options in the future.<br /> <br /> <br /> If it helps, Spinning the Web offers up to 9 experience. My idea of a Methuselah as a story character is different from a player character. If I made stats that felt appropriate then I would have a character that I would quickly get bored playing and the antagonists would get out of hand. Also, I wouldn't know where to go as far as using experience. It seems easy enough to start low and give experience out like candy if necessary to provide a boost if the characters don't feel Elder enough. The Around the Block merit helps cut out points spent on skills that don't need to be mastered and I would give 5 to 10 merit points in things that the Sanctity rule would never apply like Multilingual. In other words, I don't think for players it is that far off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T03:58:52-07:00","id":1108337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1108163#post1108163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. I think people underestimate a starting character's competence. Two dots in a skill is &quot;professional&quot; quality according to the book. How many skills is the average adult good enough at to do it professionally?</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is that two dots doesn't actually fairly represent someone doing something professionally. If I failed at doing my job as often as a 'professional' dice pool (2 Skill, 3 Att) would lead you to believe, I'd be out of work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T04:54:58-07:00","id":1108352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1108337#post1108337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue is that two dots doesn't actually fairly represent someone doing something professionally. If I failed at doing my job as often as a 'professional' dice pool (2 Skill, 3 Att) would lead you to believe, I'd be out of work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Getting one character package for free at elder char gen and then slapping additional 25exp over it would make more sense. Would be still weaksouce","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T05:49:41-07:00","id":1108360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orzhov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1108352#post1108352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting one character package for free at elder char gen and then slapping additional 25exp over it would make more sense. Would be still weaksouce</div> </div> </div> </div>I think again we're coming across the 'I think it should be like this' where 'this' is not represented by the setting but by some perception of what elders are that's been developed independently of the setting.<br /> <br /> An arc represents 75 years or so spent pursuing something away from the All Night's Society and vampire politicking. Elders start at 150 years of undeath, maybe more with some torpor. The arcs make more sense for the urban legend and Methuselah type vampires, who have been around for a long time and not the equivalent of 'two human lifetimes' of an elder in name.<br /> <br /> Basically you're expecting just being an elder to give you a lot more than the setting has always said it should. If you want an elder that is weirdly powerful with a wide variety of skills, you should not be looking at a Rank Elder, you should be looking at something closer to the aforementioned urban legend or Methuselah. Despite the complaints that Methuselah don't get a lot of special powers, they have all the special abilities of elders and four times as much Experience to work with. If for whatever reason that isn't fitting, one can always just add more Experience, such as moving everyone's equivalent Experiences up a rank, but appreciate that you're getting into homebrewing, putting your ideas into the rules, and this shouldn't necessarily be reflected in the book, as not everyone comes to the game with your views.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-27-2017, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T06:35:30-07:00","id":1108374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1108337#post1108337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue is that two dots doesn't actually fairly represent someone doing something professionally. If I failed at doing my job as often as a 'professional' dice pool (2 Skill, 3 Att) would lead you to believe, I'd be out of work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Note that you're only supposed to roll the dice when your character is in &quot;a stressful situation.&quot; The book examples for &quot;stressful situation&quot; are &quot;actively trying to tear his throat open, or demolish the building as he works.&quot; For the average person, in the average work day, they'll only rarely be rolling if they do at all. And at 4 dice in your pool or more, you have a success rate of 75% or higher.<br /> <br /> At four dice, you have a very strong chance of success under pressure. It's only in combat, or when afflicted with penalties (working in the dark and/or without tools, for example) that you need more.<br /> <br /> Once again, I think people underestimate how competent a starting character is.<br /> <br /> And with CofD's lower XP costs, I think they vastly underestimate how competent an Elder will be, by extension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T06:53:17-07:00","id":1108382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1108374#post1108374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again, I think people underestimate how competent a starting character is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Failing 25% of the time under pressure is a horrifically abysmal success rate for a 'professional'.<br /> <br /> It's possible that people are not overestimating or underestimating anything, you just might have a different bar for what counts as competence than those disagreeing with you.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1108360#post1108360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think again we're coming across the 'I think it should be like this' where 'this' is not represented by the setting but by some perception of what elders are that's been developed independently of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the fluff of this book literally portrays them as being weirdly powerful beings that barely follow the same rules as their lessers.<br /> <br /> The fluff and the mechanics do not get along. I'm fine with either interpretation, but they need to agree with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 06-27-2017, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T07:45:57-07:00","id":1108402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1108382#post1108382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Failing 25% of the time under pressure is a horrifically abysmal success rate for a 'professional'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see that as reasonable, though, depending on how you define &quot;under pressure&quot;, and also what would constitute as a failure. Some stress seems normal enough for most occupations that it shouldn't require a roll. And in many everyday situations you can just try it again if you fail, or failure doesn't matter. E.g. if I'm at work (software development) and I get stuck, I just take a break and try again ten minutes later. Or I ask for advice or consult google. My mother works at a supermarket; if she makes a mistake during the Christmas shopping ultra rush, maybe she drops an item on the floor, or forgets to say &quot;hello&quot; with a smile to customer. <br /> <br /> But the stuff you roll for in RPG's tend to have much greater ramifications for failures, or be in situations where rolling again doesn't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11756-razikale","name":"Razikale","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T08:08:28-07:00","id":1108410,"title":"","content":"Rote actions are for the small stuff like that, I happen to agree that elders should be powerful and haven't really been displayed as such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T10:55:14-07:00","id":1108447,"title":"","content":"What exactly does the Married by Blood merit offer, exactly? It doesn't bring anything new to the table, as far as I'm aware.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T11:45:48-07:00","id":1108461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1108447#post1108447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly does the Married by Blood merit offer, exactly? It doesn't bring anything new to the table, as far as I'm aware.</div> </div> </div> </div>Normally each vampire sharing a Haven has to contribute at least one dot to it to benefit from the Haven, and Retainers can't normally be shared.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T12:00:47-07:00","id":1108464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1108360#post1108360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think again we're coming across the 'I think it should be like this' where 'this' is not represented by the setting but by some perception of what elders are that's been developed independently of the setting.<br /> <br /> An arc represents 75 years or so spent pursuing something away from the All Night's Society and vampire politicking. Elders start at 150 years of undeath, maybe more with some torpor. The arcs make more sense for the urban legend and Methuselah type vampires, who have been around for a long time and not the equivalent of 'two human lifetimes' of an elder in name.<br /> <br /> Basically you're expecting just being an elder to give you a lot more than the setting has always said it should. If you want an elder that is weirdly powerful with a wide variety of skills, you should not be looking at a Rank Elder, you should be looking at something closer to the aforementioned urban legend or Methuselah. Despite the complaints that Methuselah don't get a lot of special powers, they have all the special abilities of elders and four times as much Experience to work with. If for whatever reason that isn't fitting, one can always just add more Experience, such as moving everyone's equivalent Experiences up a rank, but appreciate that you're getting into homebrewing, putting your ideas into the rules, and this shouldn't necessarily be reflected in the book, as not everyone comes to the game with your views.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is a fair interpretation of the disagreement some of us have with the number of experiences elders start with. Before A Thousand Years of Night, there was pretty much no guideline for 2e as to what elders would actually be (the experiences table in character creation wasn't very helpful in this regard). And yes, people do bring their interpretations of what elders might be like from fiction (which largely has elders being more powerful than they're represented in A Thousand Years of Night), and it is fair to draw interpretations from the fiction that Vampire: The Requiem draws inspiration from.<br /> <br /> I don't know why this impulse to label people as somehow &quot;wrong&quot; or possibly even wanting &quot;badwrongfun&quot; for having a different idea of what elders should be than the line developer and writers, to the point of trying to assert that any disagreement with elder power levels must necessarily come from outside the game entirely and have nothing to do with it, is the path you want to take, but it is really condescending, not helpful, and will only serve to further entrench people and not particularly lead to interesting discussion.<br /> <br /> And god knows I don't want to get entrenched enough that it sounds like I hate A Thousand Years of Night before I've even had a chance to read it. What I've heard of it sounds <i>really good</i>, and I will be picking it up as soon as I can (which will be later this week). But... I am allowed to have a different idea of what constitutes an elder from the writers, from the developer, and from other fans. And I would request that you not try to characterize that different idea as something bad or wrong or unfounded.<br /> <br /> Edit: And Inodiv pointed out that the perception of elders being &quot;weirdly powerful&quot; is actually in the book itself, and doesn't match the mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 06-27-2017, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T12:07:10-07:00","id":1108466,"title":"","content":"I'm unclear about Mortal Souls. They're listed among the Touchstones, and the quote, &quot;Drinking a soul is an exhilarating experience that allows the Kindred to relive the mortal\u2019s life as she sucks out his soul: a beautiful and grisly reminder of what it\u2019s like to be human&quot; makes it sound like it's meant to be a possible Touchstone. But then later it says, &quot;A diablerized mortal can never serve as Touchstone.&quot; Is the intent here that the addiction becomes a Touchstone but the victims can't be? Or is it just a cool mechanic that doesn't provide a Touchstone in any way, and if so, why is it in the Touchstones section?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T17:15:48-07:00","id":1108553,"title":"","content":"I took the Touchstone section to offer what is, is not, and sometimes is and sometimes isn't a Touchstone. With Simulacra Touchstones, it makes sense if offering the option to Diablerize mortals that it is clarified that it isn't a Touchstone. I think there are actually a couple of examples where it says that it wouldn't actually make a good Touchstone, but they still put it in the section. It was probably just a cool mechanic thought up while making Touchstones that was decided not a good example after all and they didn't want a miscellaneous rules section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T17:33:38-07:00","id":1108563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1108466#post1108466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm unclear about Mortal Souls. They're listed among the Touchstones, and the quote, &quot;Drinking a soul is an exhilarating experience that allows the Kindred to relive the mortal\u2019s life as she sucks out his soul: a beautiful and grisly reminder of what it\u2019s like to be human&quot; makes it sound like it's meant to be a possible Touchstone. But then later it says, &quot;A diablerized mortal can never serve as Touchstone.&quot; Is the intent here that the addiction becomes a Touchstone but the victims can't be? Or is it just a cool mechanic that doesn't provide a Touchstone in any way, and if so, why is it in the Touchstones section?</div> </div> </div> </div>Might be worth throwing in the errata thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T18:10:02-07:00","id":1108575,"title":"","content":"Merit 000 or 00000<br /> [Discipline] Mastery<br /> Prerequisite Blood Potency 3 and a Discipline at 5 dots.<br /> By spending 2 Vitae and a point of Willpower you can use a Discipline or preform a Clash of Wills as a Rote Action with a bonus equal to half your Blood Potency. This merit must be brought separately for each Discipline, the three dot version of this merit applies to Disciplines you can buy at in clan price and the five dot version applies to out of clan ones.<br /> Drawback: Using this merit calls deeply upon the power of the Beast, every time you use this merit roll your Humanity as a dice pool, if you fail your Beasts energies are released with the following effects, any witnesses who have any understanding of the Beast (even having witnessed Frenzy may be enough) understand that that same thing is being channeled though you, anyone who could get a Blood Sympathy connection with you understands that you are calling upon a lot of power, physics/sensitives/anyone who the ST thinks is appropriate might detect you, near by animals seek to flee and the action becomes a (one time) Braking Point at Humanity equal to your Blood Potency.<br /> <br /> I may need to edit this in the morning but is it something that gives Elders the power level they should have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T18:25:24-07:00","id":1108577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1108563#post1108563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Might be worth throwing in the errata thread?</div> </div> </div> </div> Agreed, that is confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T18:54:00-07:00","id":1108585,"title":"","content":"So based off the Coil of Quintessence, can Ordo Dracul mysteries have multiple coils to master?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T21:41:36-07:00","id":1108620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1108585#post1108585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So based off the Coil of Quintessence, can Ordo Dracul mysteries have multiple coils to master?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is how I interpreted it, I'm just wondering if we are going to see any drafts or data dumps of Elder levels of the other 2nd Ed Coils. Like Secrets of the Covenants had for Devotions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T06:30:15-07:00","id":1108737,"title":"","content":"Ok, I've read Thousand Years a few times (it was a long set of flights, blah) and will home in on one of the key points of contention in this thread: unimpressive elders, and the example threats.<br /> <br /> It could be helpful to consider the situation from the ST's perspective of player dynamics; if you want to start an elder game, or a player has a reason to be running an elder, a tool now exists canonically to do that. It's somewhat weaksauce, but why? Storytellers have a harder time on average cranking player power level <b><i>down</i></b>, versus ratcheting it or NPC power level <b><i>up</i></b>.<br /> <br /> Reading between the lines here, I view the XP for various age bands as starting points, for elders who have nominal activity cycles and don't get into extraordinary trouble or circumstances. They essentially live a life or two, erring on the side of caution and risking themselves only when necessary. I think that's fair, it meets the profile of most vampires.<br /> <br /> PCs don't do this. Players don't gather around the table week after week to discuss a few bullet-points of how they pay the bills and arrange consistent feeding patterns and ensure the security is in place. For PCs, unlife is bigger, badder and usually much more terrifying. They may stack up experiences of a lifetime within a few months of in-game play, or at least a few years.<br /> <br /> Similarly, the threats in Thousand Years are characters that are dangerous, active and antagonistic. They're made to reflect individuals who live far, far closer to the edge of destruction than any average vampire would feel comfortable with. Their experience totals reflect this. (Again, reading between the lines.) If you had a comprehensive history of Kindred, you'd see many, many characters who follow the same profiles as these threats, but are destroyed or burn out after short periods of time; the ones lucky or clever enough to keep themselves alive, while being crazy or driven enough to persist in extreme danger, end up legends whispered to terrify neonates.<br /> <br /> The downside to very high activity/danger cycles is that a character will collect a large number of enemies, faster, or end up owing many boons. Enemies, if used, restrict action and help drive conflict. Boons act as hooks to pull characters into things they otherwise would ignore. If I had a player (or NPC) that wanted to reflect the same kind of high activity, I'd houserule categories of activity that act as a multiplier, ranging from x0 to perhaps x2.5, and grant automatic backgrounds in various side-effects such as these.<br /> <br /> The fact the book does not acknowledge the activity dynamic is either a purposeful choice or an oversight, but in either case it's disappointing and a loss.<br /> <br /> On another note: what I expected and was disappointed to see absent were more of the vampiric &quot;stretch goals&quot; for unlife. Things such as Live Bait's merit above, or Devotion examples that require BP 6+ to purchase (as appeared in a few 1e supplements). Elder's don't lose powers purchased at high BP after emerging from torpor, and that's what really sets them apart. The tools to reflect this fact well are missing.<br /> <br /> I suppose the door stands open for homebrew.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 06-29-2017, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T08:07:54-07:00","id":1108762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1108737#post1108737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I've read Thousand Years a few times (it was a long set of flights, blah) and will home in on one of the key points of contention in this thread: unimpressive elders, and the example threats.<br /> <br /> It could be helpful to consider the situation from the ST's perspective of player dynamics, if you want to start an elder game, or a player has a reason to be running an elder, a tool now exists canonically to do that. It's somewhat weaksauce, but why? Storytellers have a harder time on average cranking player power level <b><i>down</i></b>, versus ratcheting it or NPC power level <b><i>up</i></b>.<br /> <br /> Reading between the lines here, I view the XP for various age bands as starting points, for elders who have nominal activity cycles and don't get into extraordinary trouble or circumstances. They essentially live a life or two, erring on the side of caution and risking themselves only when necessary. I think that's fair, it meets the profile of most vampires. <br /> <br /> PCs don't do this. Players don't gather around the table week after week to discuss a few bullet-points of how they pay the bills and arrange consistent feeding patterns and ensure the security is in place. For PCs, unlife is bigger, badder and usually much more terrifying. They may stack up experiences of a lifetime within a few months of in-game play, or at least a few years.<br /> <br /> Similarly, the threats in Thousand Years are characters that are dangerous, active and antagonistic. They're made to reflect individuals who live far, far closer to the edge of destruction than any average vampire would feel comfortable with. Their experience totals reflect this. (Again, reading between the lines.) If you had a comprehensive history of Kindred, you'd see many, many characters who follow the same profiles as these threats, but are destroyed or burn out after short periods of time; the ones lucky or clever enough to keep themselves alive, while being crazy or driven enough to persist in extreme danger, end up legends whispered to terrify neonates.<br /> <br /> The downside to very high activity/danger cycles is that a character will collect a large number of enemies, faster, or end up owing many boons. Enemies, if used, restrict action and help drive conflict. Boons act as hooks to pull characters into things they otherwise would ignore. If I had a player (or NPC) that wanted to reflect the same kind of high activity, I'd houserule categories of activity that act as a multiplier, ranging from x0 to perhaps x2.5, and grant automatic backgrounds in various side-effects such as these.<br /> <br /> The fact the book does not acknowledge the activity dynamic is either a purposeful choice or an oversight, but in either case it's disappointing and a loss.<br /> <br /> On another note: what I expected and was disappointed to see absent were more of the vampiric &amp;quot;stretch goals&amp;quot; for unlife. Things such as Live Bait's merit above, or Devotion examples that require BP 6+ to purchase (as appeared in a few 1e supplements). Elder's don't lose powers purchased at high BP after emerging from torpor, and that's what really sets them apart. The tools to reflect this fact well are missing.<br /> <br /> I suppose the door stands open for homebrew.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the book was pretty good for the most part, and I agree about the xp totals. However, I was mostly just dissapointed with some of the mechanics. I think all the devotions were pretty good, but I mostly found the covenant specific powers to be lacking; I was also hoping for some Elder scales of existing coils, but the new coil is pretty neat. I was kind of dissapointed in the lack of anything for the Invictus elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T09:31:01-07:00","id":1108792,"title":"","content":"I think there's a heck of a lot more territory that could cover &quot;nominal activity cycles&quot; than the current XP totals suggest. That is to say, you can increase the XP and still be fine. The XP totals as they have been reported are easily achievable by neonates in a neonate game, and barely reflect the kind of experience one might accrue over centuries of existence, even if not as active as your typical player characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T11:42:41-07:00","id":1108846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1108792#post1108792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's a heck of a lot more territory that could cover &quot;nominal activity cycles&quot; than the current XP totals suggest. That is to say, you can increase the XP and still be fine. The XP totals as they have been reported are easily achievable by neonates in a neonate game, and barely reflect the kind of experience one might accrue over centuries of existence, even if not as active as your typical player characters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly my point. Representing the figures in the book as a baseline from which more active and risk-taking kindred evolve to higher experiences accumulations is a fair take I think. I wish they'd just taken a sidebar to say so--or a few paragraphs even!<br /> <br /> Me? My games are all written, PbP affairs anymore, and that means you can timeline and wave a heck of a lot of stuff into the background. From there, going back over &quot;downtime&quot; between major sessions is pretty easy, you can break it apart into what looks like a session's worth of ground being covered and award nominal beats (a few) for the jump. This can work out to be a beat per year, or several depending on the amount of text that goes into it; more text == more &quot;sessions&quot;.<br /> <br /> I would have loved to see some discussion of campaign journaling, timeline-ing and the like as tools for elder campaigns that span the ages. Covering flashbacks is good, and the background web is a great idea unfamiliar to me (harkens back to Chicago by Night, a bit), but there are other, more linear approaches. The appeal of vampire to me is the ability to capture bits of history and the aching weight of years these creatures supposedly drag around. But that's me.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 06-28-2017, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T15:20:29-07:00","id":1108973,"title":"","content":"Anyone know how the Inmorata are suposed to use the Enticing merit?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#681D00\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Enticing</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Effect: Your character\u2019s seductive Beast oozes with ease and confidence. Her smoky looks tantalize the imagination. Every movement of her hands makes promises. Any rolls to invoke the seductive Beast gain the 8-again quality.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Drawback: Your character does not get the 10-again quality on any rolls to invoke or resist the monstrous or competitive Beasts.</span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Mortals can fight the Beast, but they cannot impose a Condition on the vampire.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>Do they just get 8-again when resisting a Vampire lashing out if they use Presence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T15:23:22-07:00","id":1108976,"title":"","content":"I believe it's been brought up in the errata thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T21:29:47-07:00","id":1109107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">For every Touchstone normally granted to her, either by Humanity or Merits, she instead gains two. These Touchstones only provide a +1 bonus each to detachment rolls, up to a total of +3 for three or more Touchstones.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Is there any mechanical change for Kindred, or do elders just have more touchstones to play around with? I looked in the core book, and with having more than one touchstone you're still getting +3 dice, and for having the one touchstone you're still getting +2 dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T21:37:27-07:00","id":1109108,"title":"","content":"Would a sequel be Two Thousand Years of Night? Or a Million Years of Night?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T21:40:18-07:00","id":1109109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1109108#post1109108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a sequel be Two Thousand Years of Night? Or a Million Years of Night?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it means Neolithic Vampire and Signature Settings build around Elders, I'd be down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T07:44:41-07:00","id":1109237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1109108#post1109108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a sequel be Two Thousand Years of Night? Or a Million Years of Night?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd like a Requiem Dark Ages treatment called &quot;A Thousand Years of Knights&quot;.<br /> <br /> But a &quot;Ten-Thousand Years of Nights&quot; that adds an order of magnitude to the elder supernatural powers/options would do. I think that would fix the expectations gap some of us had.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T08:56:07-07:00","id":1109255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1109237#post1109237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like a Requiem Dark Ages treatment called &quot;A Thousand Years of Knights&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did not this prequel was Souless &amp; Dead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T09:04:04-07:00","id":1109258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1109255#post1109255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did not this prequel was Souless &amp; Dead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your parsing isn't making sense there Wyrd","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T09:09:26-07:00","id":1109263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1109255#post1109255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did not this prequel was Souless &amp; Dead?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's an understandable parsing, if you've recently been thinking of the Dark Eras Companion. Anyway Wyrd, that specific Era covers the Black Death pretty well, but is a tiny slice of medieval history and/or the age of knights<br /> <br /> My main point was an amusing play on words (Night &lt;=&gt; Knight), but that aside I like the Dark Eras treatment, where an interesting time and place is extracted for serious CofD consideration. I'm just not as excited by the other splats, and would prefer more VtR materials. *shrug* YMMV<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T22:29:33-07:00","id":1109632,"title":"","content":"Now I have a copy so I won't have to react second hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T21:49:09-07:00","id":1110058,"title":"","content":"Also if I run an elder game I'll try RAW re experiences, to see how it plays out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T11:26:36-07:00","id":1110275,"title":"","content":"So I picked up ATYoN yesterday. Haven't had time to digest it fully. But I did look at the extinct clans stuff, that was the thing I was most excited about. I was... a little underwhelmed, maybe? I was hoping for write-ups in the style of the corebook, with the sections about what makes each clan cool and desirable to play, scary to others, and internally terrifying, with sample concepts and a couple pages each. Glad we got discipline and Attributes, though. <br /> <br /> I was a little disappointed that the Pijavica had the same discipline spread as the Gangrel, but after some thought, it struck me as brilliant: the Gangrel are the clan of the Beast, the Pijavica are the clan of the Blood. I also feel like they're about as close as we're getting to Tzimisce in Requiem, so I'm all for it. Would love to incorporate them into a Chronicle- maybe they aren't quite as dead as people think? Or maybe set the Chronicle in a universe where they survived into the Modern Nights, cousins and rivals to the Gangrel, and of course the darlings of the Ordo Dracul?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T12:25:14-07:00","id":1110298,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, a domain where they are resurgent, no alternate universe required.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T08:07:54-07:00","id":1110858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1110275#post1110275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was a little disappointed that the Pijavica had the same discipline spread as the Gangrel, but after some thought, it struck me as brilliant: the Gangrel are the clan of the Beast, the Pijavica are the clan of the Blood. I also feel like they're about as close as we're getting to Tzimisce in Requiem, so I'm all for it. Would love to incorporate them into a Chronicle- maybe they aren't quite as dead as people think? Or maybe set the Chronicle in a universe where they survived into the Modern Nights, cousins and rivals to the Gangrel, and of course the darlings of the Ordo Dracul?</div> </div> </div> </div>We're now anticipating the inevitable Haberdasher treatment of the Tzimisce come Pijavica, in which vicissitude 5th dot is simply their innate form and they feed targets blood in order to reshape flesh.... <br /> <br /> Surely the writers find the parallels between these guys and VtM, and some of the connections are not accidental. Most of VtM's clans show up in one form or another, reimagined, in VtR. Not a bad thing at all, and likely to scratch an itch for players who just really want to play their flesh-shaping Slavic lords of iron will. Keep in mind that even in VtM the Tzimisce were presented as a fading clan (at least, from the Camarilla's perspective of course!), so it's not a far stretch to <i><b>claim</b></i> they went extinct by the renaissance....<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T09:24:30-07:00","id":1110886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1110275#post1110275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I picked up ATYoN yesterday. Haven't had time to digest it fully. But I did look at the extinct clans stuff, that was the thing I was most excited about. I was... a little underwhelmed, maybe? I was hoping for write-ups in the style of the corebook, with the sections about what makes each clan cool and desirable to play, scary to others, and internally terrifying, with sample concepts and a couple pages each. Glad we got discipline and Attributes, though. <br /> <br /> I was a little disappointed that the Pijavica had the same discipline spread as the Gangrel, but after some thought, it struck me as brilliant: the Gangrel are the clan of the Beast, the Pijavica are the clan of the Blood. I also feel like they're about as close as we're getting to Tzimisce in Requiem, so I'm all for it. Would love to incorporate them into a Chronicle- maybe they aren't quite as dead as people think? Or maybe set the Chronicle in a universe where they survived into the Modern Nights, cousins and rivals to the Gangrel, and of course the darlings of the Ordo Dracul?</div> </div> </div> </div> No clan is so extinct that the Strix can't bring them back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T13:29:46-07:00","id":1110976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1110858#post1110858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most of VtM's clans show up in one form or another, reimagined, in VtR.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. I was struck by how much the Akhud are Assamite expies, minus all the baggage. And they even manage to fit into the &quot;archetypal vampire type&quot; VTR uses for each clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T15:05:34-07:00","id":1111029,"title":"","content":"My 2 cents:<br /> <br /> * Pick up any elder NPC from 1st Edition <b>New Orleans</b> or 2nd Edition <b>Reap the Whirlwind</b>. They total XP is far beyond the recommend XP from <b>Thousand Years of Night</b>. If you start to play with neonate and accumulate XP for a few months, it will probably result in a character with more XP than starting elder. The same elder surrounded by much more powerful NPC elders (based on NPC from the books).<br /> <br /> __<br /> <br /> And I have a question. In <b>Step 5, MERITS</b>, in page 19, it says:<br /> <br /> <i>(...)These resources double as signs of status in the Kindred community.(...) </i><br /> <br /> For me the text is not exactly clear about the benefits. You start with 20 mertis OR every dot in Haven, Herd or Feeding Grounds counts as two dots?<br /> <br /> __<br /> <br /> The rest of the book seems fine for me. I like it very much.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> PS: Sorry for any english mistakes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13644-ghostwalker","user":"Ghostwalker","date":". 07-03-2017, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13644-ghostwalker","name":"Ghostwalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T15:32:50-07:00","id":1111038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghostwalker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1111029#post1111029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[I](...)These resources double as signs of status in the Kindred community.(...) [/]<br /> For me the text is not exactly clear about the benefits. You start with 20 mertis OR every dot in Haven, Herd or Feeding Grounds counts as two dots?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I think it means that it means that an Elder with high dots in these merits is considered more influential than an Elder without or having low dots in these merits. Basically, high dots in these will have other Kindred respect you more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T15:39:17-07:00","id":1111041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1111038#post1111038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I think it means that it means that an Elder with high dots in these merits is considered more influential than an Elder without or having low dots in these merits. Basically, high dots in these will have other Kindred respect you more.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok... that makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13644-ghostwalker","name":"Ghostwalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T09:22:04-07:00","id":1111298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1110858#post1110858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We're now anticipating the inevitable Haberdasher treatment of the Tzimisce come Pijavica, in which vicissitude 5th dot is simply their innate form and they feed targets blood in order to reshape flesh....<br /> <br /> Surely the writers find the parallels between these guys and VtM, and some of the connections are not accidental. Most of VtM's clans show up in one form or another, reimagined, in VtR. Not a bad thing at all, and likely to scratch an itch for players who just really want to play their flesh-shaping Slavic lords of iron will. Keep in mind that even in VtM the Tzimisce were presented as a fading clan (at least, from the Camarilla's perspective of course!), so it's not a far stretch to <i><b>claim</b></i> they went extinct by the renaissance....<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>And here I thought you were a fan of my work, Khanwulf. Enough to want to use my Asn\u00e2m in your own chronicle. Why the sudden change of heart? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Rest assured, I have no plans on doing a conversion of the Tzimisce. Masquerade is Masquerade and Requiem is Requiem, and ne'er the twain shall meet in my conversions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T19:32:47-07:00","id":1111946,"title":"","content":"So I've only read like 2/3rds but I have to say I love the story stuff in the book. The discussion about nodes and how to introduce complications is great stuff.<br /> <br /> I don't think I'll be running an elder game, though. I've got a pretty decent neonate game that should start shortly after I move (I have been waiting so long for this move).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T23:24:22-07:00","id":1111991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1111298#post1111298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And here I thought you were a fan of my work, Khanwulf. Enough to want to use my Asn\u00e2m in your own chronicle. Why the sudden change of heart? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Rest assured, I have no plans on doing a conversion of the Tzimisce. Masquerade is Masquerade and Requiem is Requiem, and ne'er the twain shall meet in my conversions.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I would gladly read it! I'm only passing fan of <b>Requiem</b>, but in Poland we have only '<b>Masquerade, Masquerade, Masquerade</b>' all the time - showing that <b>VtM</b> 'cool Clans' can be recostructed in <b>VtR</b> by canonical factions would be GODSEND!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T00:16:50-07:00","id":1112000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1111991#post1111991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But I would gladly read it! I'm only passing fan of <b>Requiem</b>, but in Poland we have only '<b>Masquerade, Masquerade, Masquerade</b>' all the time - showing that <b>VtM</b> 'cool Clans' can be recostructed in <b>VtR</b> by canonical factions would be GODSEND!</div> </div> </div> </div>You need to stop spreading such malicious lies about Poland mate. In Poland we only have Warhammer Fantasy Roleplay 1st edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T00:30:12-07:00","id":1112001,"title":"","content":"I really thought the Long Solo stood out. Lots and lots of story hooks for my chronicles now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T01:23:13-07:00","id":1112010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orzhov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1112000#post1112000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need to stop spreading such malicious lies about Poland mate. In Poland we only have Warhammer Fantasy Roleplay 1st edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we talk about 'vampire horror RPGers' it's only <b>VtM</b> then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T01:37:40-07:00","id":1112013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1112010#post1112010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If we talk about 'vampire horror RPGers' it's only <b>VtM</b> then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I'm jokeing. I got a lot of shit from VtM fanboys(even if most of them no longer play anything) when I said I run Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T06:13:27-07:00","id":1112073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1111298#post1111298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And here I thought you were a fan of my work, Khanwulf. Enough to want to use my Asn\u00e2m in your own chronicle. Why the sudden change of heart? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Rest assured, I have no plans on doing a conversion of the Tzimisce. Masquerade is Masquerade and Requiem is Requiem, and ne'er the twain shall meet in my conversions.</div> </div> </div> </div>You misunderstand: I'm with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> here, and conversions of anything pre-existing, showing how it *could* fit in VtR, are GOOD things. VtR knows it is a spiritual child of VtM, it's written all over the terminology and tropes. The main things that were ditched were the oppressive mythology and meta-plot elements (I'm over-simplifying, don't jump on this point). <br /> <br /> There's nothing &quot;wrong&quot; with Tzimisce, Vicissitude and land-tied Slavic gentry in Eastern Europe desperately clinging to ancient rights and, um, rites, while making monsters in their basements. That's... a lot of tropes, but the bundle appeals to some for protagonists, others for antagonists. I like them as antagonists, mostly because their Discipline is burn-it-with-fire scary. But I also like re-using VtM characters to save time and create a sense of familiarity, as well as running Dark Eras/Dark Ages past chronicles.<br /> <br /> And yeah, Asnam are a go!<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T07:34:48-07:00","id":1112096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1112073#post1112073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's nothing &quot;wrong&quot; with Tzimisce, Vicissitude and land-tied Slavic gentry in Eastern Europe desperately clinging to ancient rights and, um, rites, while making monsters in their basements. That's... a lot of tropes, but the bundle appeals to some for protagonists, others for antagonists. I like them as antagonists, mostly because their Discipline is burn-it-with-fire scary. But I also like re-using VtM characters to save time and create a sense of familiarity, as well as running Dark Eras/Dark Ages past chronicles.<br /> <br /> And yeah, Asnam are a go!<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>As a guy from Poland, I really would like to see Tzimisce-like vampires without metaplot overbearings and casting them strongly as bad guys ( in Sabbath). And my Romania Ordo Dracul need's some love! Pijavica Clan sounds like could fullfil those!<br /> <br /> So who will start a mini project on this? \ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T15:05:57-07:00","id":1112362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1112073#post1112073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You misunderstand: I'm with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> here, and conversions of anything pre-existing, showing how it *could* fit in VtR, are GOOD things. VtR knows it is a spiritual child of VtM, it's written all over the terminology and tropes. The main things that were ditched were the oppressive mythology and meta-plot elements (I'm over-simplifying, don't jump on this point).<br /> <br /> There's nothing &quot;wrong&quot; with Tzimisce, Vicissitude and land-tied Slavic gentry in Eastern Europe desperately clinging to ancient rights and, um, rites, while making monsters in their basements. That's... a lot of tropes, but the bundle appeals to some for protagonists, others for antagonists. I like them as antagonists, mostly because their Discipline is burn-it-with-fire scary. But I also like re-using VtM characters to save time and create a sense of familiarity, as well as running Dark Eras/Dark Ages past chronicles.<br /> <br /> And yeah, Asnam are a go!<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Only teasing, Khanwulf. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If I ever did something that blended Masquerade and Requiem, it would be to port Masquerade clans and bloodlines and fit them into a Requiem 2e framework, and convert some of the Masquerade fluff. Gangrel, Ventrue, and Nosferatu need no conversion, and Toreador to Daeva is obvious. Tzimisce to Pijavica, Assamite to Akhud make a lot of sense. A lot of the other clans could get represented as Requiem bloodlines jumped up to the rank of a full-blown clan. <br /> <br /> And it always warms my cold, withered heart when I hear that somebody is using my conversions, whether as a PC or an NPC. Have your players had the pleasure/misfortune of meeting this Sanam yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T21:30:39-07:00","id":1112501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1112362#post1112362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assamite to Akhud make a lot of sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>OOOOHHH! AHHAHAHaha--*cough* *golf clap* Well done sir. Headcanon filed: had not made that connection yet!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1112362#post1112362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of the other clans could get represented as Requiem bloodlines jumped up to the rank of a full-blown clan.<br /> <br /> And it always warms my cold, withered heart when I hear that somebody is using my conversions, whether as a PC or an NPC. Have your players had the pleasure/misfortune of meeting this Sanam yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to think that the term &quot;clan&quot; is used by a group that is large enough in a given area to constitute a major extended familial relation, with similar blood powers and afflictions. While &quot;bloodline&quot; is the polite term for a minority distinct in powers and afflictions from the major &quot;clans&quot;. Depending on the scholarly bent of the Kindred with whom you converse, they might admit that all family lines are technically &quot;bloodlines&quot;--or not. Should you wander far enough, to where a minority group is numerous enough to form a local majority, they'll probably call themselves a Clan. And if (for example) you stand before the Keeper of Alamut, it would be wise to call the Akhud a clan--and not just a Bloodline--in case you get another night out of it.... <br /> <br /> The Sanam? Not met <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rowena\" target=\"_blank\">her</a> yet, but PCs are about to encounter the second of her assassination attempts on the presumptive next High King. Then, later in the game year, there will be a proper confrontation; &quot;killing&quot; her just, er, kicks the can down the road of course. I'll let you know when it all gets temporarily resolved--for your amusement.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T21:52:15-07:00","id":1112505,"title":"","content":"I think clan and bloodline are pretty thoroughly defined in Requiem - clans have three disciplines and a bane. Bloodlines deviate from clans, have a fourth discipline and often special devotions, and have an additional bane. A bloodline could potentially grow to be quite large, but it'd still be a bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 07-07-2017, 02:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T22:26:36-07:00","id":1112513,"title":"","content":"Correction: A Bloodline <i>always</i> has four &quot;in-clan&quot; Disciplines. In the vast majority of cases at least two of these are carried over from the parent Clan.<br /> <br /> I can also add that everyone belongs to a Clan regardless of their Bloodline-status (which affects bloodties and can be determined by tasting their Vitae), and that Bloodlines doesn't necessarily carry over from Sire to Childe (which makes <b>B</b>loodlines and <b>b</b>loodlines two different things). It would seriously kill any Bloodline's claim for Clan-hood if it turned out those from the Bloodline can induct members from one of the Clans after the embrace, or could embrace Childer without inducting them to the Bloodline.<br /> <br /> I guess that in more isolated domains it might be possible that a Bloodline styles itself as a Clan, but there'd had to be unique circumstances for that Bloodline to actually be believed, such as little to no communication with other domains (which would make at least four of the five big Covenants impossible in that particular domain).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T23:15:41-07:00","id":1112520,"title":"","content":"You're right, corrected my post.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T17:43:28-07:00","id":1113007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1112501#post1112501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OOOOHHH! AHHAHAHaha--*cough* *golf clap* Well done sir. Headcanon filed: had not made that connection yet!</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, that one came right after I connected the dots between the Tzimisce and the Pijavica. &quot;Wait, a clan of Near East origin who have diablerie playing a major role in their backstory? Hakim, you've been naughty again, haven't you?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106165-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=1112501#post1112501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sanam? Not met <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rowena\" target=\"_blank\">her</a> yet, but PCs are about to encounter the second of her assassination attempts on the presumptive next High King. Then, later in the game year, there will be a proper confrontation; &quot;killing&quot; her just, er, kicks the can down the road of course. I'll let you know when it all gets temporarily resolved--for your amusement.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wcinzmfZeCc\" target=\"_blank\">Oh, that link made my day.</a> Few things I like better than making players figuratively wet themselves- once introduced a couple NPCs who were obviously fey- one of them was a original character of my own creation whom I dubbed &quot;The Fiddler,&quot; the other was Queen-freaking-Titania herself- to a group of C:tL veterans in a D&amp;D game I ran. They proceeded to lose their minds. It was delightful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 07-07-2017, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T20:22:50-07:00","id":1113076,"title":"","content":"And all this self-referential alt-history, to return to topic, is why vampire is a hoot. Specifically, vampire that makes full use of their immortal nature to tell the stories between the stories that make up our recorded history.<br /> <br /> I laugh and clap when the CofD authors &quot;get&quot; this too, and do self-referencing touches back to Masquerade... Only, through a mirror, darkly.<br /> <br /> What other gems have we missed?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}